iner\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=303755#post303755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished the first major portion of the book - the part written in first person. Whoa.</div> </div> </div> </div>My knowledge of it's mostly secondhand and I'm probably ignorant of a common inspiration, but I'm seeing shades of DtF history in the temakh's situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T16:24:29-08:00","id":303844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=303755#post303755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished the first major portion of the book - the part written in first person. Whoa. Need to process this for a bit (and maybe go back to getting work done for a while).</div> </div> </div> </div>That last little bit, the third to last sentence of that section, really struck me. It certainly makes sense in the context of the myths from the Mummy corebook.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, all that stuff about the Rite of Return being outside of time certainly provides one easy answer to the many questions that have sprung up surrounding the timeline of the Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-05-2014, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:18:25-08:00","id":303910,"title":"","content":"I am still fairly confused at what the Keeper is. I mean, I get the tattoos/scarification thing as an art, but I feel like I'm missing something on top of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:56:00-08:00","id":303936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=303910#post303910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the tattoos/scarification thing as an art, but I feel like I'm missing something on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be. Remember, there's already a Painter, so it's less about the body modification and more about a powerful connection to the primal earth; note the references to lower animals, in particular, of which Hakkar-Zozer is the primordial keeper.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T19:24:54-08:00","id":304014,"title":"","content":"The Keeper seems to be a shaman/mad prophet/crazy street person. I see his Art as including stuff like glossolalia, frenzied dancing and drumming, self-flagellation and austerities, primal howls and screams, weird effigies made from dead things.... the kind of &quot;art&quot; that was too weird and chaotic for any of the other Shan'iatu. He's all about the irrational and instinctive, with as little mediation as possible from the &quot;higher&quot; mind.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing, for example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mIVWqn1AvAc\" data-code=\"mIVWqn1AvAc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mIVWqn1AvAc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T19:46:04-08:00","id":304064,"title":"","content":"So..I followed my DriveThru link for Book of the Deceived and went to order it....and it purchased the Mummy:The Curse core pdf I already own....<br /> <br /> I hope no one else is having this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:18:12-08:00","id":304075,"title":"","content":"Anyone willing to post some spoilers for those poor souls waiting for payday? I'd love to hear a little about each individual temakh, if that's okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:20:31-08:00","id":304078,"title":"","content":"Not tonight-I'm reading longer than I should anyways, I still have a book for class to read.<br /> <br /> I will say this. I've accused Mummy of being a big game before, but this?<br /> <br /> This is monumental. Appropriately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:22:20-08:00","id":304079,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I can drag myself away from the book for that long...<br /> <br /> The Temakh in general though cut really tragic figures. There's a first person narrative of the history of the Shan'iatu, from the perspective of one of the Temakh, that opens the book and describes the secret history of the Deceived. Really makes you feel for the poor ol' immortal sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:34:34-08:00","id":304104,"title":"","content":"Can someone spoil me on how precisely the Deceived were... y'know, deceived? And I have someone claiming that this book outright states that the Shan'iatu became the Judges; can anyone confirm or deny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:37:04-08:00","id":304106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304104#post304104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone spoil me on how precisely the Deceived were... y'know, deceived? And I have someone claiming that this book outright states that the Shan'iatu became the Judges; can anyone confirm or deny?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Free hugs. Never accept free hugs from strangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:38:25-08:00","id":304111,"title":"","content":"Seriously, I think I speak for everyone who worked on it by saying it's amazing this is finally out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:41:42-08:00","id":304116,"title":"","content":"WARNING: The following contains spoilers from the Book of the Deceived. I should have marked the entire thread a Storyteller Thread, I apologize.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They very definitely did <i>not</i> become the Judges. I don't know what that person was smoking. There's a difference between Life and Death, and that aside, the Judges were...Well, not quite the daddy's of the Shan'iatu, they definitely preceded them in an inviolable way.<br /> <br /> As for the Deceived....Well, I'll say this-The Shan'iatu on the whole got deceived twice, and the Deceived got it thrice.<br /> <br /> The third time has to do with the Rite of Return. The Restless Stars were the last to go through the entire affair, and they figured the other guilds were going to use them to ascend to Azar's side and then leave them the lowest, so they figured they'd come in as the Judges of Life <i>and</i> Death(That might be where your friend was confused, as the Shan'iatu were out to make themselves a second set). Turns out the other guilds, quite probably mostly the Su-Menent, fucked that up for them, and now the Restless star guildmasters are riding their guild.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly right on that. I'll need to go over the Judges things again, although I know for a fact that the Shan'iatu did not become the Judges we know.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304111#post304111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, I think I speak for everyone who worked on it by saying it's amazing this is finally out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I speak for everyone reading it right now that we're duely blown away by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-05-2014, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:56:12-08:00","id":304126,"title":"","content":"The book is a fantastic read so far. There are so many little elements I love to bits. I skipped ahead a little to see what their powers were like, and... wow. I've been making plans for a Deceived game to run concurrently with my current Mummy game for a while now, and after this I cannot wait to get it started. There are just so many great character concepts whirling around my head right now.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Plus, the first time my regular Mummies face off against an enemy who can literally <i>become a Shan'iatu</i> promises to be something truly great.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:03:20-08:00","id":304131,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading Book of the Deceived (except the SAS at the end). I liked it a lot, but I'll need to re-read it one or two more times before posting a review. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=303822#post303822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My knowledge of it's mostly secondhand and I'm probably ignorant of a common inspiration, but I'm seeing shades of DtF history in the temakh's situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely a few parallels, although BotD has the advantage of not adapting one of the most well known myths (and classic literature if you factor in Paradise Lost), so the story has some unexpected twists and a few more layers of ambiguity.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">At first I thought that BotD made it clear that the Shan'iatu became the Judges, then I thought it was clear that they did not. Now I think that we don't know what happened to the other Shan'iatu. Irem and the Shan'iatu were pulled down into Duat after the Rite of Return, but since no one knows what happened to Azar (aside from what Anpu says), it's hard to say whether they successfully became a new set of Judges. Seriously, I'm impressed that the the book was able to reveal so much about the Shan'iatu and Irem while still making the ultimate truths deeply ambiguous - it raises as many questions as it answers. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do have one rules/setting question (so far). Has anyone figured out where it says how to divine a person's True Name? A lot of the Utterances and Affinities reference True Names for additional effects, but I think I missed the section on how to determine that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:10:04-08:00","id":304136,"title":"","content":"No idea on the true names. I finished Chapters One and two, about a fourth of the third, and the Affinities and Utterances of the Deceived and haven't noticed that in particular. I imagine it's a matter of story.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If I've misinterpreted anything else from Chapter One, this I know I got right-the Shan'iatu are <i>not </i>the Judges we know.<br /> <br /> In fact, going straight to the beginning, the Shan'iatu are the children of the Judges. They adore and place Azar first, but they exist to serve the Judge's purposes-to prepare mankind for judgment that they might enter A'aru.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-06-2014, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:10:15-08:00","id":304137,"title":"","content":"Any tasty new deets on Ammut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:15:32-08:00","id":304138,"title":"","content":"She is quite, quite clever and manipulative, for something that embodies ravenous hunger and the end of all things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:18:16-08:00","id":304142,"title":"","content":"Ammut is a beeeeeeeitch who hmmmmm likes bananas.<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, she's terrifying.<br /> <br /> I'd say more, but I closed the book so I can go read Green Grass, Running Water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:26:31-08:00","id":304145,"title":"","content":"Ammut is a lot like the Wyrm from cWoD's Werewolf the Apocalypse, in that she embodies a natural force that has overstepped its bounds, but she's far more subtle. No Pentex, no Formori, no crazed shapeshifters. Just a few words into the itching ears of the powerful to accomplish devastating, eternal effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:28:46-08:00","id":304146,"title":"","content":"I do find it amusing how many ways there are for the Deceived to be mistaken for Serpent-Headed* in light of their turning out to <i>not even have Decrees.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* dammit why did i only just make the connection between that and &quot;I was Sutek, but so were we all&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:34:10-08:00","id":304151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304146#post304146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find it amusing how many ways there are for the Deceived to be mistaken for Serpent-Headed* in light of their turning out to <i>not even have Decrees.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* dammit why did i only just make the connection between that and &quot;I was Sutek, but so were we all&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god damnit, I missed that too.<br /> <br /> And that is rather awesome-I hadn't seen that. RIght now my mind is in pure indexing mode, so the little details are escaping me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:40:30-08:00","id":304177,"title":"","content":"Oh, I need to start indexing this stuff, but we learned a lot of tantalizing hints about sorcerers in this book. They stole secrets in the days of Irem, for instance. At some point, I should make a conspiracy theory post to catalogue what we know about these enigmatic mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:46:52-08:00","id":304184,"title":"","content":"Oh don't get me wrong, I'm digesting a fair bit of the reading. The main point of the first reading may be to just create the space in my head, but I'm still getting most of it in.<br /> <br /> But that first chapter is super dense-anyone trying to blaze through it is going to not get all the nuance. With it, most of the juicy stuff is yet to be properly chewed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:47:57-08:00","id":304185,"title":"","content":"Also of some amusement to me, given the clear devil-theming bouncing around in the gaps, is that the one Favored Attribute-pair that isn't represented is Manipulation/Wits.<br /> <br /> EDIT: More esprit d'escalier: In light of what the temakh resemble, of <i>course</i> Utterances have an Old Testament miracle flavor to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-06-2014, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T02:05:05-08:00","id":304300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304184#post304184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that first chapter is super dense-anyone trying to blaze through it is going to not get all the nuance. With it, most of the juicy stuff is yet to be properly chewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely not a super light read - I recommend reading the whole thing slowly over some time and to really digest all the details - and I read the core directly before editing as a brush up.<br /> <br /> It really is one of the best &quot;antagonist&quot; books that I've had the pleasure to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T02:34:45-08:00","id":304315,"title":"","content":"I love the fact that Seba make it possible to run mortal sorcerers, mechanics-wise, without reaching out to non-Mummy supplements. Even if a future book doesn't detail them, between the Deceived Cultist merit and Seba we have all the rules we need to drop humans with magical powers into a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:07:08-08:00","id":304368,"title":"","content":"This book has a great mood to it. The whole imagery of 'dark starlight' really sells it to me. This book isn't about stars burning brightly in the night sky - it's about the dark shadows swirling in between them. The text is very evocative, and the art is fucking terrifying - nightmare stuff.<br /> <br /> In case anyone was wondering: <i>the Deceived are assholes</i>.<br /> <br /> They're just jealous. They found out something was going to happen and they were going to be short-handed, so they planned on exploiting the situation and screw everyone <i>else</i> over, but then they got called out on it so they're just pissed. They don't hate the Arisen so much as they hate those who created them.<br /> <br /> It's like if you and your friends were planning to prank a pizza shop into delivering you a ton of pizza for the price of one. But you, the guy soon to be Deceived, were conspiring to eat all of that pizza before your friends. Then they found out and made sure you got no pizza at all. So now you're planning to burn down the pizza shop.<br /> <br /> Like...<i>what</i>? What the hell kind of <i>asshole </i>are you?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:13:58-08:00","id":304376,"title":"","content":"Finally getting a chance to dig into it without skimming like I did when I first purchased. It certainly casts a new light on the nature of Shan'iatu and the Judges of Life. I wasn't expecting the relationship between the Judges of Life and the Shan'iatu like I did but it's presentation gives me all sort of interesting ideas on how to incorporate this information into personal ideas about what constitutions &quot;The Principal&quot;. The Deceived strike me less as assholes and more ones who got bit on wanting the best of both worlds. Desiring the earthly pleasures they learned to enjoy while wanting to serve the purpose of their original masters in some sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:14:37-08:00","id":304377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304368#post304368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book has a great mood to it. The whole imagery of 'dark starlight' really sells it to me. This book isn't about stars burning brightly in the night sky - it's about the dark shadows swirling in between them. The text is very evocative, and the art is fucking terrifying - nightmare stuff.<br /> <br /> In case anyone was wondering: <i>the Deceived are assholes</i>.<br /> <br /> They're just jealous. They found out something was going to happen and they were going to be short-handed, so they planned on exploiting the situation and screw everyone <i>else</i> over, but then they got called out on it so they're just pissed. They don't hate the Arisen so much as they hate those who created them.<br /> <br /> It's like if you and your friends were planning to prank a pizza shop into delivering you a ton of pizza for the price of one. But you, the guy soon to be Deceived, were conspiring to eat all of that pizza before your friends. Then they found out and made sure you got no pizza at all. So now you're planning to burn down the pizza shop.<br /> <br /> Like...<i>what</i>? What the hell kind of <i>asshole </i>are you?!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more the Temakh than the Deceived themselves, although the confluence of the two makes that distinction more than a little superfluous. That said, I can't help but feel sorry for them, and the whole of the Shan'iatu for that matter. Ammut played them off against one another, and the gods, to perfection.<br /> <br /> I've been mulling over the Seba section a little more, and it really struck me as odd that there were multiple examples of Seba in the 1-3 range, but none for 4-5. Was this intentional? It feels at odds with the regular relic section in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-06-2014, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:20:24-08:00","id":304379,"title":"","content":"This is only a partial reasoning, but do note that 5 dot seba are required for Deceived-apotheosis. I forgot the term - I did the initial perusal of the entirety and now comes the detailed read","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:25:18-08:00","id":304385,"title":"","content":"I found it very ironic that the Shan'iatu were the first that tried to shirk their duty to the Judges. Ohh poor me I can't go to paradise, but I'm immortal and have unlimited power and will rule the mortals and be the most privileged in the living world, but nooo I have to be an ashole to the mortals because the Judges are assholes too(I can't go to Paradise like the mortals, so the Judges are cruel because of that and I have to be cruel) and everytime will try to shirk my duties and give up my privileged position in Irem and try and go to Paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:25:40-08:00","id":304386,"title":"","content":"There also aren't any samples that make use of the idea of &quot;conditionally sacrifice the Seba for a greater effect&quot;, which is a bit of a shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:56:42-08:00","id":304396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304379#post304379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only a partial reasoning, but do note that 5 dot seba are required for Deceived-apotheosis. I forgot the term - I did the initial perusal of the entirety and now comes the detailed read</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we will see some 4-5 dots Seba in Sothis Ascends. But they definitely exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T04:24:37-08:00","id":304427,"title":"","content":"Maybe someone else has picked up on this, but have I missed the bit detailing the actual Deceived? The first chapter explains the Sha'niatu, the Sixth Guild temakh, and the Rite of Return for the Arisen. What I think I'm missing is the detailing of how the deceived temakh performed the spell needed to bind themselves into Deathless servants. I feel like I missed a link somewhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T04:39:41-08:00","id":304440,"title":"","content":"Some of the bits in the book, the Painter's write-up for example, makes it seem pretty clear that they were right bang in the middle of carrying out the Rite of Return when they were betrayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T07:33:59-08:00","id":304554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304427#post304427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someone else has picked up on this, but have I missed the bit detailing the actual Deceived? The first chapter explains the Sha'niatu, the Sixth Guild temakh, and the Rite of Return for the Arisen. What I think I'm missing is the detailing of how the deceived temakh performed the spell needed to bind themselves into Deathless servants. I feel like I missed a link somewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>My exegesis is that the Priests of the Shell (Su-Menet) gave the Akhem-Urtu guildmasters a corrupt version of the Rite of Return that dispersed their spirits into those they performed the Rite on. <br /> However, it's just as possible that the Akhem-Urtu Shan'iatu's attempt to claim the power of life and death simply interacted poorly with the Rite devised by Ammut and/or the Su-Menet and backlashed pretty badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T07:59:11-08:00","id":304581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304554#post304554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My exegesis is that the Priests of the Shell (Su-Menet) gave the Akhem-Urtu guildmasters a corrupt version of the Rite of Return that dispersed their spirits into those they performed the Rite on.</div> </div> </div> </div>My inclincation is towards this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:14:28-08:00","id":304664,"title":"","content":"By the way, it has been really nice that the presense of Fate has been expanded upon in Deceived , they are even more connected to it than the Arisen and they Apotheosis is essentially becoming servants of this cosmic force rather than a entity like the Judges and the Temakh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:17:22-08:00","id":304746,"title":"","content":"I am pleased to see that my favorite line that I wrote for the book made it in, speaking to the absolute immortality of the Deceived. Hope you all enjoy the implications.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Should the world be scoured so clean of life and remnants thereof that no trace of humanity remains, then the eternal echoes of the mummy\u2019s True Name throughout the cosmos shall determine where the sahu must resurrect again and again until the end of time. Some future epoch may see lonely Restless Stars rise upon the burning sands of Mars, staring up at the red giant filling most of the sky as they struggle to hold onto fading recollections of Earth like worn tombstones scoured of epitaphs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, on the same track, consider what sorts of ways the Affinity Eternal Legend might replenish a Deceived's cult if humanity were to go extinct. &quot;It has not yet come to pass that no possible cultists could be recruited by Fate within the usual time intervals for the Affinity. Should that tragedy become so, providence is patient and inevitable; it will, in the fullness of time, find replacements somehow.&quot; Yes, that means that one mummy manifesting this magic could potentially ensure that sapient life evolved anew upon the planet to eventually worship her. Or it could also mean that the magic could drag alien explorers from other worlds to unearth and give worship to a dead god of a dead planet.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:20:37-08:00","id":304749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304746#post304746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pleased to see that my favorite line that I wrote for the book made it in, speaking to the absolute immortality of the Deceived. Hope you all enjoy the implications.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Should the world be scoured so clean of life and remnants thereof that no trace of humanity remains, then the eternal echoes of the mummy\u2019s True Name throughout the cosmos shall determine where the sahu must resurrect again and again until the end of time. Some future epoch may see lonely Restless Stars rise upon the burning sands of Mars, staring up at the red giant filling most of the sky as they struggle to hold onto fading recollections of Earth like worn tombstones scoured of epitaphs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, on the same track, consider what sorts of ways the Affinity Eternal Legend might replenish a Deceived's cult if humanity were to go extinct. &quot;It has not yet come to pass that no possible cultists could be recruited by Fate within the usual time intervals for the Affinity. Should that tragedy become so, providence is patient and inevitable; it will, in the fullness of time, find replacements somehow.&quot; Yes, that means that one mummy manifesting this magic could potentially ensure that sapient life evolved anew upon the planet to eventually worship her. Or it could also mean that the magic could drag alien explorers from other worlds to unearth and give worship to a dead god of a dead planet.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I love that. Keep it up. Getting BotD when I can. I haven't played Mummy yet, but I've gotten all the books even if I can only read them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:21:24-08:00","id":304752,"title":"","content":"I also liked the almost-explicit statement that the Deceived's relationship with their cultists is a lot less healthy than other Arisen.<br /> <br /> With other Arisen, it's more like a group of mentally healthy teenagers under an overbearing and frequently absent but caring and devoted parent, while in the case of the Restless Stars, it's...a cult, in the modern definition (ie, emotionally abused minions serving a master that honestly doesn't care that much about them). The Shan'iatu Virtues are cool too, shows just how alien Irem was as a civilization, but one that was still made by humans (or mostly-human demigods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:27:33-08:00","id":304759,"title":"","content":"The cultists of the Deceived get a lot more out of their servitude, but it is certainly servitude. Yet it is also an act of true and meaningful faith to worship one of the Restless Stars. If you believe hard enough in the right god, death cannot end you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:36:19-08:00","id":304781,"title":"","content":"This made me bust out laughing when I read it in Chapter 3:<br /> &quot;This isn\u2019t even our final form.&quot;<br /> \u2014 Charles Darwin<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/386/280/bd8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:40:09-08:00","id":304801,"title":"","content":"I used to think the Judges are cruel but now I just think it's necessity. They're distant automatons of Fate, you can't blame them really.<br /> <br /> The temakh are like the Judges if they <i>care</i><i>d</i> about things on a personal, emotional, human level - except all they could feel is lying manipulation and vengeful anger","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:44:30-08:00","id":304804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304801#post304801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to think the Judges are cruel but now I just think it's necessity. They're distant automatons of Fate, you can't blame them really.<br /> <br /> The temakh are like the Judges if they <i>care</i><i>d</i> about things on a personal, emotional, human level - except all they could feel is lying manipulation and vengeful anger</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what happens when you get the peanut butter of human pettiness into the cosmic deliciousness of Fated chocolate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:59:28-08:00","id":304832,"title":"","content":"(As a disclaimer of sorts as I've only read Chapter 1 as of this post)<br /> <br /> I kinda like the ambiguity of Chapter 1 in regards to the use of the term &quot;Judges&quot; actually.<br /> <br /> The 42 Judges mentioned in that chapter as the &quot;mothers and fathers&quot; of the Shan'Iatu are celestial beings seemingly on par but distinct and different in nature form the Gods. They reside in the paradise that mortals go to after Duat has purged them of sins.<br /> <br /> The 42 Judges that the Arisen seem to be bound too dwell in Duat and at least from a human viewpoint don't really seem to be living in paradise.<br /> <br /> I think the whole thing leaves it nicely &quot;up-to-the-ST&quot; about <b>IF</b> the Judges of Duat (the realm of the dead) are the same Judges as that the Shan'Iatu served, or the result of the Rite of Return (which by the way it being sorta &quot;timeless&quot; makes a lot of the head scratching over &quot;when&quot; it happened make a lot more sense now) and the Shan'Iatu getting to have their cake and eat it too. In so far as they finally got to get into the afterlife and got take Irem with them.<br /> <br /> I'm also kinda interested in what's up with the other Nameless Gods now. Anpu and Azar are accounted for nicely. There is also that line about Sutek. Still leaves the Nameless Lion, Bull and Falcon to be accounted for. Hmmm...wonder if that will be covered by Dreams of Avarice or if its another thing left for the ST to decide.<br /> <br /> Liked that Anpu and not Ammut seems to be in command of the Demons of Duat. I had a pet theory they served either the Judges or the Devourer. I did not see them serving Anpu so its a pretty awesome surprise for me. Does make me wonder how Shezmu fits into all that then? Is he Anpu's &quot;dragon&quot; so to speak?<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one that got a big idiot grin when the last bit about the Heretic was mentioned? Considering that Mummy is a pretty dark game, its nice to have a &quot;big good&quot; in the background. Plus his quest for Apotheosis and the results of him achieving it seem to be far more far reaching then I maybe first envisioned &quot;he's an artist&quot; indeed. Honestly, he's starting to get up to Count F***ing Dracula and Verney levels of cannon NPC popularity for me now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:09:01-08:00","id":304859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304801#post304801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to think the Judges are cruel but now I just think it's necessity. They're distant automatons of Fate, you can't blame them really.<br /> <br /> The temakh are like the Judges if they <i>care</i><i>d</i> about things on a personal, emotional, human level - except all they could feel is lying manipulation and vengeful anger</div> </div> </div> </div>You know Book of the Deceived and they description of the Temakh made me really want to get the Book of Going Westard and have all the Judges detailed. I hope people buy the hell out of Deceived and Sothis so Onyx Path feel confident to write it. Book of the Deceived made me fall even more in love with the cosmology and history of the Arisen, I want to know more about the other Shan'iatu, Judges, Fate and the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:21:29-08:00","id":304873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304746#post304746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pleased to see that my favorite line that I wrote for the book made it in, speaking to the absolute immortality of the Deceived. Hope you all enjoy the implications.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Should the world be scoured so clean of life and remnants thereof that no trace of humanity remains, then the eternal echoes of the mummy\u2019s True Name throughout the cosmos shall determine where the sahu must resurrect again and again until the end of time. Some future epoch may see lonely Restless Stars rise upon the burning sands of Mars, staring up at the red giant filling most of the sky as they struggle to hold onto fading recollections of Earth like worn tombstones scoured of epitaphs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, on the same track, consider what sorts of ways the Affinity Eternal Legend might replenish a Deceived's cult if humanity were to go extinct. &quot;It has not yet come to pass that no possible cultists could be recruited by Fate within the usual time intervals for the Affinity. Should that tragedy become so, providence is patient and inevitable; it will, in the fullness of time, find replacements somehow.&quot; Yes, that means that one mummy manifesting this magic could potentially ensure that sapient life evolved anew upon the planet to eventually worship her. Or it could also mean that the magic could drag alien explorers from other worlds to unearth and give worship to a dead god of a dead planet.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thundercats makes so much sense now.....Thinking over it I really am wondering now just who the Judges in Duat are and what the hell happened to the other Shan'iatu, what are the Nameless Gods and what is the nature of this Fate that has so strong an agency with mummies?... What has really impressed me about the book is the interlocking pieces of creepy that all help to make up just how the Deceived are these boogey-men in the World of Darkness without it simply being body horror squick. From being eternal monstrosities of Fate, whose terror can evoke worship, the Cthulhu F'tang! of Al-Runihura, to the way new powers like Ever-Dying Name, Horror Among Horrors, Unspeakable Name, Word of Life, their version of Blessed is the God-King, Call Down the Black Huriyah, Forgetting the Name(throwback!), etc. Everything just wraps together to make the Restless Stars SCARY even to things that go bump in the night. Wow.<br /> <br /> There was one paragraph though I'm not sure how I will take it in regards to fitting in the mummy into the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Arisen do not fear much in the World of Darkness, nor should they. The awesome power of the Rite of Return endows them with miracles that frequently dwarf the magic of other supernatural beings, to say nothing of how mummies utterly dominate mortals and ghosts alike. Magicians are both fascinated and horrified at the casual ways Arisen tear the universe's laws asunder as they reach back through time and across the vaults of the heavens. Even the most terrible demons and glorious spirits give the Arisen a wide berth, recognizing the manifest godhood of Irem's immortals and their connection to a Fate beyond the divine machinery of the cosmos.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-06-2014, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:30:22-08:00","id":304883,"title":"","content":"You know I reread the first chapter that contained the history of the Deceived and I thought ocurred to me, maybe they weren't really Deceived at all, at least not by the other Shan'iatu but rather just by Ammut. Maybe they really became the Judges of Life and Death, a part of their Soul(the Ren) staying in the world of the living and the rest went to Duat and became the Judges of Death like the others, they just don't know that. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:34:42-08:00","id":304906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304873#post304873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Arisen do not fear much in the World of Darkness, nor should they. The awesome power of the Rite of Return endows them with miracles that frequently dwarf the magic of other supernatural beings, to say nothing of how mummies utterly dominate mortals and ghosts alike. Magicians are both fascinated and horrified at the casual ways Arisen tear the universe's laws asunder as they reach back through time and across the vaults of the heavens. Even the most terrible demons and glorious spirits give the Arisen a wide berth, recognizing the manifest godhood of Irem's immortals and their connection to a Fate beyond the divine machinery of the cosmos.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing that came to mind was the <b>Book of the Dead</b> and how Mummies would be treated in the Underworld (which is mentioned in <b>Book of the Deceived</b>, implying that it's kinda separate from Duat - especially given the newly revealed natures of Duat) in regards to the Dead Laws.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking they're given grudging respect. &quot;Ugh, I <i>hate</i> Mummies coming down here thinking like they're so high and mighty.&quot; &quot;Yeah, man, I know. But what can you do?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:40:10-08:00","id":304913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304906#post304906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing that came to mind was the <b>Book of the Dead</b> and how Mummies would be treated in the Underworld (which is mentioned in <b>Book of the Deceived</b>,<b> implying that it's kinda separate from Duat</b> - especially given the newly revealed natures of Duat) in regards to the Dead Laws.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking they're given grudging respect. &quot;Ugh, I <i>hate</i> Mummies coming down here thinking like they're so high and mighty.&quot; &quot;Yeah, man, I know. But what can you do?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We've known that for a long time. For me it's a lot of figuring out just how to fit it all into the cosmology canon I want in my head. I know that certain bits of BotD is going to change how I have mages who get to study mummies are going to react to them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:50:55-08:00","id":304918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=303936#post303936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might be. Remember, there's already a Painter, so it's less about the body modification and more about a powerful connection to the primal earth; note the references to lower animals, in particular, of which Hakkar-Zozer is the primordial keeper.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He's a blasphemous, horrifying John Muir! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT - I'm only partially joking. Hakkar-Zozer appears to me to embody the concept of the natural world as its own inherent beauty, unadorned by civilization or ornamentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 11-06-2014, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:55:15-08:00","id":304922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304883#post304883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I reread the first chapter that contained the history of the Deceived and I thought ocurred to me, maybe they weren't really Deceived at all, at least not by the other Shan'iatu but rather just by Ammut. Maybe they really became the Judges of Life and Death, a part of their Soul(the Ren) staying in the world of the living and the rest went to Duat and became the Judges of Death like the others, they just don't know that. Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would explain why there are 42 Judges of Duat, not 35 (assuming that the Judges the Arisen serve are the former Shan'iatu, and not the &quot;real&quot; celestial Judges).<br /> <br /> Although, given the fact that the Rite of Return apparently is outside of time somehow, maybe there is no distinction between the two sets of Judges. Did the Judges self-create themselves through the Shan'iatu? Hmmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:58:33-08:00","id":304923,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...going back to the storyteller section of the Core book to check some facts on the Heretic and Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Now I'm trying to figure out how the &quot;Ascension of Azar&quot; with the help of the other Nameless Gods with the Ladder of Set might fit in with the the new information we have from the Deceived book. Are they referring to the same event, or does this imply that Azar got out of Duat and that the Deceived never knew about it. Or the former could just be a myth and parable to help people on the way to Apotheosis (which is more likely I guess). <br /> <br /> Heretic = shadow of a divine ruler.<br /> <br /> So the Heretic is literally known by that name because he's been given it by true-name-magic (or he claimed it once he knew its &quot;celestial name&quot;). As it its kinda impossible that the Arisen Guilds could have come to any other title for him. Which suggests Fate is involved. <br /> <br /> Apotheosis is then a &quot;reflected&quot; divinity? In fact moving away from divinity and towards a more &quot;mortal&quot; existence? This would seem to support the other fluff and mechanics we have on the subjects from the core and guildhalls. <br /> <br /> God now I really can't wait for Dreams of Avarice, so many new questions to get answered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:02:31-08:00","id":304927,"title":"","content":"I agree with others that this is a very dense book, and is going to take awhile to unravel, but so far, it's incredible. Well done to the authors!<br /> <br /> So many questions:<br /> <br /> 1) I think the only purely mechanical question I have concerns the Memory 8 sin for Deceived. It mentions that vigorously pursuing your temakh's goals is a sin against Memory. However, later in that same section, I believe it mentions that vigorously pursuing your temakh's goals can grant you a reset on your Descent with no Memory penalty. How are these reconciled?<br /> <br /> 2) I lied; one more mechanical question. It's noted that magic requiring knowledge of a target's True Name doesn't work well (or at all) on mummies, whose True Names are kept by the Judges or the temakhs. How does this reconcile with something like the Echoes of the Rattled Chains Affinity, which suggests that it can target mummies to determine information about them, despite requiring knowledge of their True Names?<br /> <br /> 3) I can't wait to see what seba of ranks 4 and 5 can do. Speaking of which, the temakh descriptions discuss various avenues to seba that each temakh apparently favors (such as inspiration, insight, etc.) Do you think these influence the kind of seba that a given Deceived can find and bind, or are they more along the lines of descriptions of where and how each temakh's Deceived is likely to find artistic seba, without limiting what such seba actually can do?<br /> <br /> 4) Are the illustrations in each temakh section a sample of a Deceived who belongs to that temakh, or somehow a representation of the temakh themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 11-06-2014, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:04:24-08:00","id":304929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304923#post304923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm...going back to the storyteller section of the Core book to check some facts on the Heretic and Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Now I'm trying to figure out how the &quot;Ascension of Azar&quot; with the help of the other Nameless Gods with the Ladder of Set might fit in with the the new information we have from the Deceived book. Are they referring to the same event, or does this imply that Azar got out of Duat and that the Deceived never knew about it. Or the former could just be a myth and parable to help people on the way to Apotheosis (which is more likely I guess).<br /> <br /> Heretic = shadow of a divine ruler.<br /> <br /> So the Heretic is literally known by that name because he's been given it by true-name-magic (or he claimed it once he knew its &quot;celestial name&quot;). As it its kinda impossible that the Arisen Guilds could have come to any other title for him. Which suggests Fate is involved.<br /> <br /> Apotheosis is then a &quot;reflected&quot; divinity? In fact moving away from divinity and towards a more &quot;mortal&quot; existence? This would seem to support the other fluff and mechanics we have on the subjects from the core and guildhalls.<br /> <br /> God now I really can't wait for Dreams of Avarice, so many new questions to get answered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling that Sothis will have more information on Apotheosis and Fate. And in the final adventure we will probably meet the Heretic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:13:48-08:00","id":304936,"title":"","content":"I wonder what category of relic the Heart Stones relic empowering the Martense tomb actually is. It doesn't seem to be a seba, since it is a physical set of stones and not a thought-concept.<br /> <br /> EDIT - On a different topic, I guess this book puts paid to the idea that the Shan'iatu were ancient mages or something similar. It appears that they never were human to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:39:23-08:00","id":304959,"title":"","content":"It seems like BotD has succeeded in completely confusing me when it comes to Mummy's cosmology/mythology just in time for my to have thought I'd figured it out. Heck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:44:45-08:00","id":304962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304913#post304913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've known that for a long time. For me it's a lot of figuring out just how to fit it all into the cosmology canon I want in my head. I know that certain bits of BotD is going to change how I have mages who get to study mummies are going to react to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own interpretation of the cosmology is based on the understanding that ghosts are different from souls in the World of Darkness.<br /> Ghosts go to the Underworld when they can no longer manifest in Twilight or in the material world.<br /> Duat is where souls go for judgement (after which the worthy souls may go on to A\u2019aru.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:20:52-08:00","id":304984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304832#post304832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liked that Anpu and not Ammut seems to be in command of the Demons of Duat. I had a pet theory they served either the Judges or the Devourer. I did not see them serving Anpu so its a pretty awesome surprise for me. Does make me wonder how Shezmu fits into all that then? Is he Anpu's &quot;dragon&quot; so to speak?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anpu seems like Duat's supervisor and janitor. The Judges, for all intents and purposes, do their jobs but only their jobs. With the death(?) of Azar, he's work load increase and as a result, is pretty pissed about that fact in regards to the temakh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:25:35-08:00","id":304986,"title":"","content":"I really like how this book plays up the Nameless Gods. I feel like they kind of got glossed over in the core book in favor of the Judges (by necessity), but the interactions of the opening chapter narrator with Azar and Anpu were awesome (especially Anpu; what a badass). Ammut just keeps getting more and more terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 11-06-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:34:09-08:00","id":305014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304927#post304927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with others that this is a very dense book, and is going to take awhile to unravel, but so far, it's incredible. Well done to the authors!<br /> <br /> So many questions:<br /> <br /> 1) I think the only purely mechanical question I have concerns the Memory 8 sin for Deceived. It mentions that vigorously pursuing your temakh's goals is a sin against Memory. However, later in that same section, I believe it mentions that vigorously pursuing your temakh's goals can grant you a reset on your Descent with no Memory penalty. How are these reconciled?</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't meant to be reconciled. It's the same for the Arisen regarding the Judges, both the Temakh and the Judges don't want their servants to reclaim Memory and become independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:35:32-08:00","id":305015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304986#post304986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like how this book plays up the Nameless Gods. I feel like they kind of got glossed over in the core book in favor of the Judges (by necessity), but the interactions of the opening chapter narrator with Azar and Anpu were awesome (especially Anpu; what a badass). Ammut just keeps getting more and more terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tough there's not any mention of the other Nameless Gods. Wonder if they have any direct role at all regarding the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:40:26-08:00","id":305019,"title":"","content":"I wondered if the woman that was sacrificed to take Azar to Duat eventually became the Isis analogue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:41:07-08:00","id":305022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305014#post305014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They aren't meant to be reconciled. It's the same for the Arisen regarding the Judges, both the Temakh and the Judges don't want their servants to reclaim Memory and become independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just not clear on whether, functionally speaking, slavishly doing the will of your temakh is a Memory sin or not, based on what I quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:06:10-08:00","id":305044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304927#post304927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I think the only purely mechanical question I have concerns the Memory 8 sin for Deceived. It mentions that vigorously pursuing your temakh's goals is a sin against Memory. However, later in that same section, I believe it mentions that vigorously pursuing your temakh's goals can grant you a reset on your Descent with no Memory penalty. How are these reconciled?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I screwed up. I'll try to get that errata fixed. Good catch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304927#post304927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I lied; one more mechanical question. It's noted that magic requiring knowledge of a target's True Name doesn't work well (or at all) on mummies, whose True Names are kept by the Judges or the temakhs. How does this reconcile with something like the Echoes of the Rattled Chains Affinity, which suggests that it can target mummies to determine information about them, despite requiring knowledge of their True Names?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some TN magic works normally on mummies. Some is harder. Some doesn't work at all. The magic itself specifies which of the three by noting additional resistance or immunity, if applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304927#post304927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I can't wait to see what seba of ranks 4 and 5 can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hopefully soon you will get to see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304927#post304927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, the temakh descriptions discuss various avenues to seba that each temakh apparently favors (such as inspiration, insight, etc.) Do you think these influence the kind of seba that a given Deceived can find and bind, or are they more along the lines of descriptions of where and how each temakh's Deceived is likely to find artistic seba, without limiting what such seba actually can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:27:27-08:00","id":305060,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm increasingly convinced that Sekhem is Pyros, Fate is the Principle, and the Shan'iatu are fallen qashmallim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:31:49-08:00","id":305061,"title":"","content":"So guys what is your favorite Temakh so far? I'm torn between The Dancer and The Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:37:29-08:00","id":305064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305060#post305060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm increasingly convinced that Sekhem is Pyros, Fate is the Principle, and the Shan'iatu are fallen qashmallim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I kinda like this - especially since mortal Alchemists in Promethean 2e have a greater role now. Perhaps, they have somewhat in common with our mysterious mortal Sekhem wielding sorcerers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:50:47-08:00","id":305075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304913#post304913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've known that for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except we really haven't. They've always been distinct in my head-canon, but not everyone was so convinced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305061#post305061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So guys what is your favorite Temakh so far? I'm torn between The Dancer and The Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Painter and the Keeper","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:23:51-08:00","id":305091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305075#post305075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except we really haven't. They've always been distinct in my head-canon, but not everyone was so convinced.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Painter and the Keeper</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a conversation a long long time back in which it was mentioned that Duat, if you had to put it somewhere was &quot;in&quot; the Lower Depths and that Mummies really don't do much in the Underworld proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:38:23-08:00","id":305098,"title":"","content":"What do people think of the Poet? (He was the one I did.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:15:40-08:00","id":305118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305060#post305060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm increasingly convinced that Sekhem is Pyros, Fate is the Principle, and the Shan'iatu are fallen qashmallim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I severely doubt that <i>qashmallim</i> can fall at all, let alone that such an event is the origin of the Shan'iatu. Fate from <i>Mummy</i> seems to be more <i>Changeling</i>'s Wyrd than anything else. Mortal sorcerers stealing Sekhem and mortal alchemists stealing Pyros is worth a look, however.<br /> <br /> If anything, it feels like <i>Mummy </i>and <i>Geist </i>tread increasingly similar waters. I'm getting the feeling that the temakh are simply what happens when something a whole lot more powerful than your average mortal dies and winds up as a geist, while Ammut is feeling increasingly like the source of the Underworld's &quot;gravity&quot; (almost like an nWoD take on Oblivion/Grandmother).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:20:13-08:00","id":305120,"title":"","content":"We almost never write anything in a game as a subset of another game's ideas, because that would do a disservice to whatever we are working on. The exceptions are extremely limited and in the case of Mummy, nonexistent. Stitch things together as you like but rest assured that a game's concept is pretty much never a relabeled part of another game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:20:36-08:00","id":305121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305098#post305098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the Poet? (He was the one I did.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that he prefer to express itself in blood and tears. It's terryfing that he wants its poets to essently be hollowed out and just do oration for oration sake(becoming maniac), essently denying then the inspirations that they bring to others, his mummies essently become like machines that just repeat verses and can't appreciate the beauty of poetry themselves.<br /> Also he got one of the best illustrations of the Temakhs along with the Painter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:24:30-08:00","id":305124,"title":"","content":"Yeah, his illustration is awesome.<br /> <br /> I really like the fact that he claims dominion over... pretty much all speech. Better yet, he manages to do so without overlapping into the territory of any of the other Temakh. I'd have thought, before reading, that doing so would clash with the Philosopher at the very least, but they actually managed to carve out their own niches quite nicely (with the Poet grabbing a pretty damned big niche).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:52:39-08:00","id":305136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305120#post305120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We almost never write anything in a game as a subset of another game's ideas, because that would do a disservice to whatever we are working on. The exceptions are extremely limited and in the case of Mummy, nonexistent. Stitch things together as you like but rest assured that a game's concept is pretty much never a relabeled part of another game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I stitch things together so I can use cool ideas from gamelines that (for one reason or another) I'm not able to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:40:13-08:00","id":305164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305098#post305098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the Poet? (He was the one I did.)</div> </div> </div> </div>He and the Singer are my favorites at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:53:24-08:00","id":305181,"title":"","content":"The Poet, The Dancer, and The Keeper all vie for my top spot. <br /> <br /> Shout out to The Keeper for making me completely retool one of my Sesha-Hebsu as an Akhem-Urtu of his.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:12:47-08:00","id":305186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305060#post305060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm increasingly convinced that Sekhem is Pyros, Fate is the Principle, and the Shan'iatu are fallen qashmallim.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:26:34-08:00","id":305196,"title":"","content":"It's really interesting just how militant the Movements are, especially in light of how often I've fielded questions about the Mummy core to the nature of &quot;But where's the fighting Guild?&quot; Every single one of the major Movements is dedicated to something's destruction. The Scions of the Emerald Ankh and the Tomb Legion each offer advantages to direct combat. The Deceived really aren't taking their betrayal lying down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:39:25-08:00","id":305202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305121#post305121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked that he prefer to express itself in blood and tears. It's terryfing that he wants its poets to essently be hollowed out and just do oration for oration sake(becoming maniac), essently denying then the inspirations that they bring to others, his mummies essently become like machines that just repeat verses and can't appreciate the beauty of poetry themselves.<br /> Also he got one of the best illustrations of the Temakhs along with the Painter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't want its chosen to lose the ability to appreciate art. What it wants is for its Deceived to be so appreciative of oration that it fills every corner of their souls with divine rapture. It wants them able to appreciate so much beauty that the beauty must flow from them unceasingly. It is the relentlessly beautiful verse that displaces what is unimportant. Also, its art does indeed rock.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:43:16-08:00","id":305204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305124#post305124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, his illustration is awesome.<br /> <br /> I really like the fact that he claims dominion over... pretty much all speech. Better yet, he manages to do so without overlapping into the territory of any of the other Temakh. I'd have thought, before reading, that doing so would clash with the Philosopher at the very least, but they actually managed to carve out their own niches quite nicely (with the Poet grabbing a pretty damned big niche).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a poet. I knew how big that slice needed to be. (Also: I was much more concerned with treading on the Singer than the Philosopher, for what it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:44:18-08:00","id":305205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305164#post305164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He and the Singer are my favorites at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm delighted to hear that. Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:46:02-08:00","id":305207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305181#post305181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Poet, The Dancer, and The Keeper all vie for my top spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>What puts the Poet there for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:46:46-08:00","id":305208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305204#post305204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a poet. I knew how big that slice needed to be. (Also: I was much more concerned with treading on the Singer than the Philosopher, for what it's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I assumed it was natural for the Singer to focus on the voice, where the Poet focusses on the words. Didn't seem quite as pressing an overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:54:28-08:00","id":305212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305202#post305202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't want its chosen to lose the ability to appreciate art. What it wants is for its Deceived to be so appreciative of oration that it fills every corner of their souls with divine rapture. It wants them able to appreciate so much beauty that the beauty must flow from them unceasingly. It is the relentlessly beautiful verse that displaces what is unimportant. Also, its art does indeed rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I've misinterpreted this line : &quot;To be hollowed by poetry is to be hallowed by poetry...&quot;<br /> I think that is the line that represent the temakh better then: &quot;..and those who speak the greatest words must be undone and consumed by their craft.&quot;<br /> Obsession only in their art at exclusion of everything else is pretty terryifing too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 11-06-2014, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T20:20:19-08:00","id":305221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305205#post305205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm delighted to hear that. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly the same reason the Cahalith are my favorite Werewolf auspice: lorehounds and performers have a special place in my heart in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T20:34:08-08:00","id":305245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305208#post305208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I assumed it was natural for the Singer to focus on the voice, where the Poet focusses on the words. Didn't seem quite as pressing an overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rhythmic words emerge from the mouth and miracles follow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T20:34:40-08:00","id":305246,"title":"","content":"At some point, I really do want to sit down and write out a few variations of the Seba responsible for the Beast in Cursed Necropolis D.C.<br /> <br /> On a side note, it's interesting to see that it's impossible for Seba to spawn Amkhat. The Temakh actually had a point when they were talking about the superiority of their own magic compared to that of their brothers and sisters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-06-2014, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T21:00:59-08:00","id":305268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305212#post305212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I've misinterpreted this line : &quot;To be hollowed by poetry is to be hallowed by poetry...&quot;<br /> I think that is the line that represent the temakh better then: &quot;..and those who speak the greatest words must be undone and consumed by their craft.&quot;<br /> Obsession only in their art at exclusion of everything else is pretty terryifing too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is terrifying.<br /> <br /> I'm bipolar and creating books often leaves me manic until I crash and temporarily collapse. I don't eat. In that state, I don't sleep, and I am relentlessly creative. For one book, I did this routine until I got so sick that I was throwing up blood. Another time left me convulsing on the bathroom floor from caffeine overdose. Rinse. Repeat. Etc. I wanted my temakh to follow in those footsteps, to be rooted in an all-too-human madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T21:22:09-08:00","id":305288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305268#post305268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is terrifying.<br /> <br /> I'm bipolar and creating books often leaves me manic until I crash and temporarily collapse. I don't eat. In that state, I don't sleep, and I am relentlessly creative. For one book, I did this routine until I got so sick that I was throwing up blood. Another time left me convulsing on the bathroom floor from caffeine overdose. Rinse. Repeat. Etc. I wanted my temakh to follow in those footsteps, to be rooted in an all-too-human madness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Creativity is one hell of a drug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:14:21-08:00","id":305336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305268#post305268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is terrifying.<br /> <br /> I'm bipolar and creating books often leaves me manic until I crash and temporarily collapse. I don't eat. In that state, I don't sleep, and I am relentlessly creative. For one book, I did this routine until I got so sick that I was throwing up blood. Another time left me convulsing on the bathroom floor from caffeine overdose. Rinse. Repeat. Etc. I wanted my temakh to follow in those footsteps, to be rooted in an all-too-human madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus-and I thought I got self-destructive with writing.<br /> <br /> I mean, I do, but wow.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I really loved the Poet for relation too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:33:33-08:00","id":305361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305202#post305202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't want its chosen to lose the ability to appreciate art. What it wants is for its Deceived to be so appreciative of oration that it fills every corner of their souls with divine rapture. It wants them able to appreciate so much beauty that the beauty must flow from them unceasingly. It is the relentlessly beautiful verse that displaces what is unimportant. Also, its art does indeed rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>The art WAS impressive, and I say this as a person who doesn't usually think about art. The biggest thing that came across to me on the nature of the Temakh is that they all have a primordial feel. Mummy in general has done a very good job of making the reader feel as if the trappings of the setting are the hoary past, but Deceived hit a chord on that mark. To harken to an earlier post. What really has impressed me about this book is where it has a less is more approach. As an creeky old CWoD person I'm aware of and owned a number of books that went front and center with the body horror, squick angle to try to generate it's horror. While Deceived has some aspects of body horror, what really stood out to me is that it wasn't what was front and center on the horror angle. Instead BotD has a sense of DOOM! as the angle of it's horror. As as a Lovecraft fan, I applaud you all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-07-2014, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:45:58-08:00","id":305368,"title":"","content":"Doom isn't Lovecraft and neither are the Deceived. They're alien spirits, okay, but they were set to watch over mankind and made to look like them as well. Their motives are definitively human in nature.<br /> <br /> The Deceived will find you, and they will kill you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:49:02-08:00","id":305370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305368#post305368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doom isn't Lovecraft and neither are the Deceived. They're alien spirits, okay, but they were set to watch over mankind and made to look like them as well. Their motives are definitively human in nature.<br /> <br /> The Deceived will find you, and they will kill you</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what you mean by doom isn't Lovecraft. All I know is that reading some of his dream cycle era stuff evokes a lot of stuff I felt while reading the book and that is good enough for me. In fact I just got done at work reading a story that is basically a template for a basic &quot;People steal relic from tomb, bad things happen to them while dread and fear of what is coming after them haunts them.&quot; story by Lovecraft. So what is and isn't Lovecraft....um yeah okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-07-2014, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:03:22-08:00","id":305379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305368#post305368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doom isn't Lovecraft and neither are the Deceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of the chapter header-quotes are from Thomas Ligotti.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Ligotti\" target=\"_blank\"><i>I would advise you to look up that name and refrain from needless pedantry.</i></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:42:18-08:00","id":305408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305379#post305379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the chapter header-quotes are from Thomas Ligotti.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty as charged.<br /> <br /> While I don't think the game's cosmic horror side was particularly subtle in the corebook, I would say that the Deceived material is certainly the place where it really just fesses up to it, no doubt. I wanted the world of <b>Mummy</b> to be its own thing, its own tone and aesthetic space, but it does have its influences.<br /> <br /> C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:42:37-08:00","id":305409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305370#post305370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what you mean by doom isn't lovecraft. All I know is that reading some of his dream cycle era stuff evokes a lot of stuff I felt while reading the book and that is good enough for me. In fact I just got done at work reading a story that is basically a template for a basic &quot;People steal relic from tomb, bad things happen to them while dread and fear of what is coming after them haunts them.&quot; story by Lovecraft. So what is and isn't Lovecraftian....um yeah okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>We got Alien gods drama, summonable yog-sothoths, opening areas beyond reality to let...things in, Forgotten bestial ancestry, &quot;The Stars are right!&quot; on so many of the spells...<br /> <br /> Mummy is pimping the crap out of the cosmic horror trope to the point where I have wonder if it's doing a better job at it than Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T03:36:29-08:00","id":305482,"title":"","content":"Well, despite my best efforts, it looks like character creation for my Deceived game won't be taking place for another week. Ah well, I get another chance to reread the book a few times.<br /> <br /> The big thing on my mind at the moment is Seba, and the artists that create it. It feels like Seba are a whole lot more common than relics, given that the default assumption seems to be that each Deceived could have multiple. At the very least, there's a lot less competition for them, and their locations can be found a bit more easily than miscellaneous relics. So I feel like a large stable of floating Seba would be a good thing to have in the game, along with plentiful artists of every variety from which the players can refill their Ren pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T03:59:41-08:00","id":305491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305409#post305409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We got Alien gods drama, summonable yog-sothoths, opening areas beyond reality to let...things in, Forgotten bestial ancestry, &quot;The Stars are right!&quot; on so many of the spells...<br /> <br /> Mummy is pimping the crap out of the cosmic horror trope to the point where I have wonder if it's doing a better job at it than Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've missed out on some many of the middle release Mage books at this point that I wouldn't even have a point of reference sadly. It was pretty much, get corebook. Ignore Mage for a long time. Return to the NWoD while Exalted was on hiatus. Get Left Handed Path and Imperial Mysteries, instantly love Mage again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T04:43:09-08:00","id":305532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305491#post305491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've missed out on some many of the middle release Mage books at this point that I wouldn't even have a point of reference sadly. It was pretty much, get corebook. Ignore Mage for a long time. Return to the NWoD while Exalted was on hiatus. Get Left Handed Path and Imperial Mysteries, instantly love Mage again.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big one would be Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss, which is the big book of Abyssal intrusions. Runners-up would be Night Horrors: The Unbidden, which is the big book of dangerous magical stuff, and.Boston Unveiled, which offers an Abyssal entity in the form of a timeline, and its extremely nasty cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T05:38:48-08:00","id":305572,"title":"","content":"I didn't say <b>Mummy</b> wasn't Lovecraft, and when I said, &quot;Doom isn't Lovecraft&quot; I didn't mean that Lovecraft doesn't do doom. I meant that, thematically, doom isn't something only Lovecraft did, so I'm perplexed why Lovecraft typically comes up whenever there's doom. It's not as if he's the only author of horror ever. Then I was just trying to distinguish a difference between the Deceived's very human motivations and the similarly 'Lovecraftian' alien horrors who very rarely express drives such as revenge.<br /> <br /> To the first point, about how indeed <b>Mummy</b> has a lot of influence from Lovecraft, you can just read what I posted in a <b>Mage</b> thread a few weeks ago:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277130-abyss-and-cthulhu-mythos?p=281546#post281546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<b>Mummy</b> comes across to me as the game for the more Lovecraftian creatures, or at least what decades of Lovecraft theme park versions have been made out to be. There's even a power that lets a group of Mummies summon/transform into Nyarlathotep</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305379#post305379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Ligotti\" target=\"_blank\"><i>I would advise you to look up that name and refrain from needless pedantry.</i></a></div> </div> </div> </div>So I'd advise you to read my admittedly short post a bit more carefully, and then maybe you won't spoil another one of your own with your trademark passive aggressiveness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T05:40:03-08:00","id":305573,"title":"","content":"On Lovecraft; Not quite within his themes to qualify as part of the cosmic horror genre, but yeah, Deceived are rocking the tropes pretty hard. They call upon dead stars, they're obsessed with the madness of art that touches on things beyond human ken, the world they live in is far stranger than what anyone can know, they will exist unto the end of the universe...<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for the fundamentally understandable motives and aspects of the temakh, they'd be full representatives of an uncaring, amoral universe hostile to humans simply because we can't adapt to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T05:52:15-08:00","id":305598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304664#post304664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, it has been really nice that the presense of Fate has been expanded upon in Deceived , they are even more connected to it than the Arisen and they Apotheosis is essentially becoming servants of this cosmic force rather than a entity like the Judges and the Temakh.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of my favorite parts of the book. An Arisen goes through Apotheosis and gets to become a (souped-up) mortal again, eventually to die and go to A'aru. A Deceived Ascends to basically become the Eternal Champion, serving Fate and wielding the power of the stars and pure creativity to set things right, presumably throughout the universe, until the end of time itself. Wow.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Ascension of Deceived, I may have missed this, but do such Deceived get to create their own seba, in the same way that Arisen who go through Apotheosis can create their own relics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 11-07-2014, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T05:55:47-08:00","id":305599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305336#post305336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus-and I thought I got self-destructive with writing.<br /> <br /> I mean, I do, but wow.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I really loved the Poet for relation too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The good news is that's behind me. I got the help (and meds) I needed to create without self-destruction. The Poet was a reminder to me of where I came from and what I must never let happen again. It's my dark side personified, which seemed apt for a horror game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T05:58:52-08:00","id":305607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305409#post305409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">summonable yog-sothoths</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, shoggoths really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:16:02-08:00","id":305616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305598#post305598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Deceived Ascends to basically become the Eternal Champion, serving Fate and wielding the power of the stars and pure creativity to set things right, presumably throughout the universe, until the end of time itself. Wow.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Ascension of Deceived, I may have missed this, but do such Deceived get to create their own seba, in the same way that Arisen who go through Apotheosis can create their own relics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deceived become angels of Fate. It's important to note that they don't set things right so much as they set things as they were meant to be. They're agents of course correction in a messed-up universe. They might be there to save you. They might be there to kill you. And yes, their scope is universal. When the Earth is ashes, their duty will remain. They are so much bigger than this world. It is only one step on their slow march to the end of time.<br /> <br /> An Arisen in Apotheosis is self-determining and a creature of limited time. He can make relics because he is fundamentally mortal and because he is a master of his corner of the world. On a long enough time frame, he will die and stay dead. His only near-immortal legacy is to bring more magic into the world.<br /> <br /> A Restless Star who has attained Apotheosis does not get to create relics. His existence is to serve the music of the spheres, not write his own melody. He is eternal, and his legacy is one of submission to Fate for all time. He will bear witness to relics coming and going. He will hold the stars in his hands and feel them slip from his fingers, only to gather anew the fruits of the Great Beyond when the time is right. He feels relics as a numinous pulse of the living universe, but he does not partake of their making. The magic he is connected to is infinitely greater than him. Fate provides. Fate takes away. Fate is inscrutable. Fate is.<br /> <br /> Does that rationale make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","user":"Nephilpal","date":". 11-07-2014, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:36:12-08:00","id":305623,"title":"","content":"\u200bAren't the Judges agents of Fate as well? How does Deceived-Apotheosis differ than a standard Arisen serving the Judges in that regard? Or...is that the point?<br /> <br /> What makes the Apotheosis of the Deceived so much greater in scope? For the Arisen, it's the mortal soul freeing itself from the Judges. But what in the Rite primed the mortal souls of the Deceived to have the possibility of becoming Fate's agents? The temakh were cosmic agents of Fate, but the Deceived Apotheosis casts them out of their bodies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:39:45-08:00","id":305624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305616#post305616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that rationale make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. And I realize that Fate's goals aren't necessarily sunshine and roses. If Fate needs an alien civilization destroyed, an Ascended Deceived is going to bring terrible eldritch power to bear against that civilization until it's ruined. I hear power chords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 11-07-2014, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:47:11-08:00","id":305633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305246#post305246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point, I really do want to sit down and write out a few variations of the Seba responsible for the Beast in Cursed Necropolis D.C.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to figure out how the Ash and Thunder Qigong works. That strikes me as a 4 or 5 dot seba, considering that it apparently kills the beneficiary after 108 days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:51:11-08:00","id":305637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305616#post305616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Arisen in Apotheosis is self-determining and a creature of limited time. He can make relics because he is fundamentally mortal and because he is a master of his corner of the world. On a long enough time frame, he will die and stay dead. His only near-immortal legacy is to bring more magic into the world.<br /> <br /> A Restless Star who has attained Apotheosis do not get to create relics. His existence is to serve the music of the spheres, not write his own melody. He is eternal, and his legacy is one of submission to Fate for all time. He will bear witness to relics coming and going. He will hold the stars in his hands and feel them slip from his fingers, only to gather anew the fruits of the Great Beyond when the time is right. He feels relics as a numinous pulse of the living universe, but he does not partake of their making. The magic he is connected to is infinitely greater than him. Fate provides. Fate takes away. Fate is inscrutable. Fate is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, the Deceived really do get the short end of the deal. They cannot escape slavery, ever. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:55:46-08:00","id":305642,"title":"","content":"I want to make sure I understand how the kepher process for finding seba works. As I read the book:<br /> <br /> 1) There's a general kepher roll that anyone can attempt that requires lengthy astrological divination, a clear view of the night sky (or its equivalent), a specific Occult Specialty, etc. Get cracking on those star-charts!<br /> <br /> 2) Fate can intercede and grant anyone a passive kepher roll that doesn't require the Occult Specialty, the ritual, or the night sky. You just have a hunch.<br /> <br /> 3) Deceived, specifically, have a much easier time finding seba than anyone else. They can choose to roll their Sekhem as the kepher dice pool instead of the normal pool (if their Sekhem is higher), don't need minimum Occult ratings or Specialties, special rituals, the night sky, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:59:06-08:00","id":305645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305637#post305637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, the Deceived really do get the short end of the deal. They cannot escape slavery, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that when the universe is no more and Fate itself is accomplished, the Ascended Deceived will get to go wherever everyone else went. Kind of like the difference between elves and men in Middle-Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T07:51:28-08:00","id":305700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305623#post305623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAren't the Judges agents of Fate as well? How does Deceived-Apotheosis differ than a standard Arisen serving the Judges in that regard? Or...is that the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I would really want to know more about the Judges relationship to Fate. What would they demand the Arisen to do besides the collecting of the Relics and the business of their Guilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T07:54:49-08:00","id":305705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305624#post305624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does. And I realize that Fate's goals aren't necessarily sunshine and roses. If Fate needs an alien civilization destroyed, an Ascended Deceived is going to bring terrible eldritch power to bear against that civilization until it's ruined. I hear power chords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tough Fate wouldn't probably ask for bad things as frequently as the Temakh as it's a impersonal entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:09:40-08:00","id":305734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305700#post305700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I would really want to know more about the Judges relationship to Fate. What would they demand the Arisen to do besides the collecting of the Relics and the business of their Guilds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it all depends on what the Judges that the Arisen serve actually are. If the opening narration is credible, the &quot;celestial&quot; Judges who gave rise to the Shan'iatu appeared to be agents of Fate. Whether or not they are the same Judges who send Arisen out into the world to collect relics is an interesting question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:18:11-08:00","id":305759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305623#post305623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAren't the Judges agents of Fate as well? How does Deceived-Apotheosis differ than a standard Arisen serving the Judges in that regard? Or...is that the point?<br /> <br /> What makes the Apotheosis of the Deceived so much greater in scope? For the Arisen, it's the mortal soul freeing itself from the Judges.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you mean by so much greater in scope. As my sidebar indicates, there are pros and cons to each form of Apotheosis. Can you clarify your question?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305623#post305623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut what in the Rite primed the mortal souls of the Deceived to have the possibility of becoming Fate's agents? The temakh were cosmic agents of Fate, but the Deceived Apotheosis casts them out of their bodies</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's easy. Fate did. For reasons known only to Fate. Apparently, Fate apparently doesn't want its agenda for the Deceived who walk the right path filtered through once-human godmonsters. Likely there are reasons that won't ever be known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:19:58-08:00","id":305760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305637#post305637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, the Deceived really do get the short end of the deal. They cannot escape slavery, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they are blessed to always have purpose. It depends on your point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:25:27-08:00","id":305766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305642#post305642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to make sure I understand how the kepher process for finding seba works. As I read the book:<br /> <br /> 1) There's a general kepher roll that anyone can attempt that requires lengthy astrological divination, a clear view of the night sky (or its equivalent), a specific Occult Specialty, etc. Get cracking on those star-charts!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. This requires <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305642#post305642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Fate can intercede and grant anyone a passive kepher roll that doesn't require the Occult Specialty, the ritual, or the night sky. You just have a hunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, using the ritual kepher dice pool, and you still need Occult 3+ or this won't happen to you. Also, Arisen and Shuankhsen probably won't ever get these flashes, what with Fate not wanting seba going into Duat or the Devourer's jaws. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305642#post305642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Deceived, specifically, have a much easier time finding seba than anyone else. They can choose to roll their Sekhem as the kepher dice pool instead of the normal pool (if their Sekhem is higher), don't need minimum Occult ratings or Specialties, special rituals, the night sky, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deceived get to use the ritual dice pool or Sekhem, whichever is higher, and can do the kepher roll instantly with no ritual or trait requirements.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:29:19-08:00","id":305769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305645#post305645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that when the universe is no more and Fate itself is accomplished, the Ascended Deceived will get to go wherever everyone else went. Kind of like the difference between elves and men in Middle-Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if they tell themselves that. Guess they'll have to wait and see. Given that all Deceived are bound to this universe inexorably (Apotheosis or not), my interpretation of the rules I wrote are that they will simply cease to be along with the universe. On the longest of time scales, they are ultimately mortal in a way that other beings aren't. Their story has soooo many chapters, but it concludes with The End.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:32:54-08:00","id":305772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305624#post305624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does. And I realize that Fate's goals aren't necessarily sunshine and roses. If Fate needs an alien civilization destroyed, an Ascended Deceived is going to bring terrible eldritch power to bear against that civilization until it's ruined. I hear power chords.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;recall the primal myths about Great Old Ones who filtered down from the stars&quot; -- H.P. Lovecraft</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T08:59:34-08:00","id":305782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305734#post305734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it all depends on what the Judges that the Arisen serve actually are. If the opening narration is credible, the &quot;celestial&quot; Judges who gave rise to the Shan'iatu appeared to be agents of Fate. Whether or not they are the same Judges who send Arisen out into the world to collect relics is an interesting question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, you are right, there is a line in the Deceived that sugests the Judges the Arisen serve are not the ones that created the Shan'iatu: &quot;We would teach the secrets we had learned, but we would teach the law of the Judges of Death we would become, not the starry wisdom of our mothers and fathers&quot;<br /> The Judges that created the Shan'iatu seen to be forces that dwell among the cosmos, not the Judges that the Arisen know that punish certain sins. It's seens that the Judges that the Arisen know were doctrine constructed by the Shan'iatu, that maybe the Rite of Return made into being or transformed the Shan'iatu into.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T09:05:54-08:00","id":305801,"title":"","content":"&quot;The greatest seba can alter the destiny of a planet in ways that are as glorious as they are potentially apocalyptic.&quot;<br /> <br /> In my head, I see the Aether from the Marvel movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T09:06:45-08:00","id":305802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305760#post305760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they are blessed to always have purpose. It depends on your point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. My personal point of view is that being mortal, and being free to choose one's own fate, is better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:15:01-08:00","id":305990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305801#post305801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The greatest seba can alter the destiny of a planet in ways that are as glorious as they are potentially apocalyptic.&quot;<br /> <br /> In my head, I see the Aether from the Marvel movies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to show you what I meant. Soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:45:23-08:00","id":306013,"title":"","content":"Looking over the document, I keep seeing hints of projects of the temakh to free themselves from the mortals that they are trapped in but a lot of them are never full realized, even in the movements. Very odd. I kinda expected movements about them hunting each other, working on networking minds, etc, etc. Projects that will eventually free the temakh and discard the mortal like one discards rotten clothes.<br /> <br /> The other thing is I am extremely confused upon the fact that former shapeshifting creatures really give a crap about the sex of the body that they and the mortal are now trapped in. Providing that the story in the first section is valid, A few of the temakh had female forms themselves before the Rite which adds to the confusion (not to mention the number of active Deceived who are female without the temakh beating them over the head over just their sex.).<br /> <br /> Which leads me to the idea that most of the conflict comes from the mortal's unfamiliarity with being the other sex hindering the temakh's plans and projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:16:10-08:00","id":306038,"title":"","content":"I propose that the 'demons' Marco Singe references in his vision are in fact the Shan'iatu. I don't assume Singe had a perfectly accurate story ; the authenticity of his sources must be questioned as must his own personal interpretations. Sometimes, he seems to confuse the Shan'iatu with angels, which can either be interpreted as 'of course' or ridiculous. That said, his vision fits pretty closely with Mummy as we've seen it.<br /> <br /> <i><b>'The God Machine built our world as a resting place for its first children, whom men called angels or ancient ones. After a time, the ancients desired servants to dwell with them, servants who walked upright and had pleasing shapes, and who could speak. They sent the proper prayer-signals to the god-machine and were granted leave to do so. First the ancient Ones took the beasts of the field and granted them the knowledge to speak and walk. But these animals retained there wildness and did not make good servants. They grew wicked and violent, and were cast into the wilderness. They were the second children, whom men called demons.'</b></i><br /> <br /> Note - the text establishes two 'races' here, but they both look very similar. It's notable that the ability to speak is something inherent and critical to design (Names?). Likewise, the Shan'iatu... from the text... seem very violent and impulsive, even somewhat insane.<br /> <br /> Further evidence...<br /> <br /> <i><b>'... and some of the men began to wonder, 'Why do the ancients spend their days in rest while we must toil without relief? Why do the ancients enjoy the pleasures of this city when it is our labors that built it? And so resentment rose among the Third Children. They made the proper calculations and sent the prayer-signals to the coordinates of the God Machine, saying, 'We are your children, too. It is not right that we be enslaved. Will you not look on us with favor?'<br /> <br /> And they recieved this answer - 'What rises must fall. What has fallen may rise again'.<br /> <br /> The men of the city debated for seven years. Finally, they decided that it was the will of the God Machine that they raise themselves from slavery. Determined to kill the Ancients and take their place as the favored of the God Machine, the men of the city plotted carefully. When the time came, they fell upon the Ancient Ones in their sleep, murdering them with there own weapons and devices in a single night of betrayal.'</b></i><br /> <br /> This closely follows the narrative of a Shana'Iatu betrayal in Book of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> And a final thought provoking quote...<br /> <br /> <i><b>'The Angel then bade me to warn mankind of the hidden forces that seek to thwart the destiny of the Third Children. Their handiwork appears again and again throughout history. Regard the mighty sphinx of Egypt. Recent studies of the water erosion on its rocky surface indicate that the monument dates back to the days when the Sahara was green and lush....&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> ... it's heavily hinted that the Sahara was established in the battle with the first Amkhata, so this is a little timeline info! But, Singe continues on...<br /> <br /> <i><b>'... Far older than the pyramids it guards, the Sphinx comes from a time close to the fall of the Ancients. The second children roamed freely through the world then, greater than man in power and knowledge. The demons shaped primitive man into a civilization that revered them as Gods. But their hubris was against the will of the God Machine, and they failed. The great civilizations of Egypt, Sumer and Babylonia rose later from the dim memories of that failure, revering Gods with the forms and features of beasts. The Egyptians called the proto-kingdoms that preceded them the First Time, or age of Osiris, and considered it the source of all wisdom and knowledge.'</b></i><br /> <br /> So my final theory IS!...<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu are the second children. If one is to believe Marco Singe, they were initially 'uplifted' animals given human shapes and immense power/intellect. Interesting when one considers the fact they are unable to go where human souls go...<br /> <br /> ... and even more chilling, is it possible the Third Children (humanity) didn't properly interpret the God-Machine's reply?<br /> <br /> Consider the statement - 'What rises must fall. What has fallen may rise again'.<br /> <br /> Was the Machine helping them?... or merely telling them the inevitable future?...<br /> <br /> For Irem fell. And what has fallen may rise again.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:23:35-08:00","id":306041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306013#post306013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking over the document, I keep seeing hints of projects of the temakh to free themselves from the mortals that they are trapped in but a lot of them are never full realized, even in the movements. Very odd. I kinda expected movements about them hunting each other, working on networking minds, etc, etc. Projects that will eventually free the temakh and discard the mortal like one discards rotten clothes.</div> </div> </div> </div>What hints do you see?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306013#post306013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing is I am extremely confused upon the fact that former shapeshifting creatures really give a crap about the sex of the body that they and the mortal are now trapped in. Providing that the story in the first section is valid, A few of the temakh had female forms themselves before the Rite which adds to the confusion (not to mention the number of active Deceived who are female without the temakh beating them over the head over just their sex.).</div> </div> </div> </div>When writing, I was instructed by CAS that all the temakhs were originally male, though I made the Poet no longer have gender now. It means that you always feel unease if any part of you is female (either your original body or your current one) due to dissonance with the temakh. In the case of the Poet, it doesn't matter what your gender is; you always get the dissonance unease because you are flesh and not made of words. That is why the section on gender issues is there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306013#post306013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leads me to the idea that most of the conflict comes from the mortal's unfamiliarity with being the other sex hindering the temakh's plans and projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the reason I was told to write. The temakhs are a patriarchy from which you cannot escape unless you shut them up by attaining Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:26:29-08:00","id":306043,"title":"","content":"Piff, the God-Machine and its cosmology were not factored at all into the design of Mummy. Any connections you want to draw are yours to create, but there is no hidden connection intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:30:56-08:00","id":306048,"title":"","content":"I'd also like put forth the very real possibility that Marco Singe <i>was fucking insane</i>, ruined by exposure to the Machine. There's no evidence to suggest he's right in his story, particularly now that we <i>have</i> God-Machine demons. That means there's equally no evidence to even begin tying it to Mummy.<br /> <br /> Nice try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2014, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:36:10-08:00","id":306049,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that this piece of fiction in the 1ed corebook was just meant to be just an evocative piece of fiction, there wasn't any intention to actually to have a God-Machine present in the gamelines, so it didn't factor what is it today any the other future gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:43:11-08:00","id":306052,"title":"","content":"The theatricality would lead me to think that Piff probably knows all this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:01:04-08:00","id":306063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306043#post306043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piff, the God-Machine and its cosmology were not factored at all into the design of Mummy. Any connections you want to draw are yours to create, but there is no hidden connection intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally understood!<br /> <br /> It's really cool, however, that simply by coincidence a few common elements can be found. I don't imagine they're intentionally designed but it's certainly a fun Easter egg for the people that go looking for it!<br /> <br /> These are some fun ways that one can interpret the Singe prophesy in a Mummy context - you don't even really have to presume a real God Machine, ultimately, if you want. Singe could just be nuts!... but even still, all the mention of a 'Wicked Kingdoms of proto-egyptians' fits pretty well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:52:53-08:00","id":306113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306041#post306041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What hints do you see?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">So we remade the Remet in our image. We made them<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">suffer, but we taught them our divine arts, assembling<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">guilds of mortals, each under the direction of seven<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">Shan\u2019iatu overlords.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\"><u><i><b>Our brothers and sisters</b></i></u> taught lesser magic, collecting<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">Sekhem from living Creation. They summoned metal<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">from shattered stone and inscribed the shape of beasts<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">on tablets. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> A little while later:<br /> <br /> &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\"><u><i><b>our brothers and sisters</b></i></u> no longer looked to us for<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">guidance \u2014 they forgot that the Nomenclature existed<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">before all tools. They ruled the sacred state through the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">power of their guilds.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">As we debated, I suspected that certain brothers and<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">sisters knew more about the Rite of Return than what<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">they spoke. For the fist time, I distrusted other students<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">of the Nomenclature. The Dancer had spoken with<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">the Shell masters before, when they proposed creating<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">replacements for the Remet. <u><i><b>She </b></i></u>smiled and moved<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">beautifully, and admitted nothing, but was adamant that<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">we support the Rite of Return, and assure the guilds of our<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleBT-Roman\">loyalty</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> So in the tale, you have informal information that some of the other guild members have at least taken up a female persona or identity and in the final case where the Dancer is outright stated was female in life. This could be passed off as unreliable narration but I can't help but wonder. After all, a few of the Judges have what would be considered feminine characteristics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306041#post306041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the reason I was told to write. The temakhs are a patriarchy from which you cannot escape unless you shut them up by attaining Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I would have to chalk the first parts as unreliable narrations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:59:26-08:00","id":306119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305572#post305572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say <b>Mummy</b> wasn't Lovecraft, and when I said, &quot;Doom isn't Lovecraft&quot; I didn't mean that Lovecraft doesn't do doom. I meant that, thematically, doom isn't something only Lovecraft did, so I'm perplexed why Lovecraft typically comes up whenever there's doom. It's not as if he's the only author of horror ever. Then I was just trying to distinguish a difference between the Deceived's very human motivations and the similarly 'Lovecraftian' alien horrors who very rarely express drives such as revenge.<br /> <br /> To the first point, about how indeed <b>Mummy</b> has a lot of influence from Lovecraft, you can just read what I posted in a <b>Mage</b> thread a few weeks ago:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I'd advise you to read my admittedly short post a bit more carefully, and then maybe you won't spoil another one of your own with your trademark passive aggressiveness</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit of false dichotomy. Lovecraft doesn't have to do exclusively a story of an impending doom, and it would be a bit odd to think so. In particularly, I had just read the story The Hound(1922) by Lovecraft, not my first reading, but over the weeks leading up to Halloween I dove back into his writing on my Kindle. Many aspects of that story in particular started floating into my brain as I read the book. A bit of friendly advise. Spend less time attempting to correct people on what you feel is and isn't Lovecraftian, and perhaps spend more time interacting positively with your fellow game fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:07:28-08:00","id":306124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306013#post306013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda expected movements about them hunting each other, working on networking minds, etc, etc. Projects that will eventually free the temakh and discard the mortal like one discards rotten clothes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna happen. By rights, the souls of those seven guildmasters should have been obliviated; what they got instead was the life of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Now they're stuck.<br /> <br /> C.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:10:58-08:00","id":306127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306124#post306124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not gonna happen. By rights, the souls of those seven guildmasters should have been obliviated; what they got instead was the life of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Now they're stuck.<br /> <br /> C.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But hey, at least they're stuck in eternals rather than mere immortals. Yay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:22:18-08:00","id":306132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305782#post305782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, you are right, there is a line in the Deceived that sugests the Judges the Arisen serve are not the ones that created the Shan'iatu: &quot;We would teach the secrets we had learned, but we would teach the law of the Judges of Death we would become, not the starry wisdom of our mothers and fathers&quot;<br /> The Judges that created the Shan'iatu seen to be forces that dwell among the cosmos, not the Judges that the Arisen know that punish certain sins. It's seens that the Judges that the Arisen know were doctrine constructed by the Shan'iatu, that maybe the Rite of Return made into being or transformed the Shan'iatu into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the impression that I got was that the Judges of Duat are not the Judges that made the Shan'iatu. Though what exactly the Nameless Gods are and how they fit into things I still don't really know or get. To call the NWoD's hoary history gloriously freaky would be an understatement it would seem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:28:27-08:00","id":306135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306119#post306119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a bit of false dichotomy. <b>Lovecraft doesn't have to do exclusively a story of an impending doom, and it would be a bit odd to think so</b>. In particularly, I had just read the story The Hound(1922) by Lovecraft, not my first reading, but over the weeks leading up to Halloween I dove back into his writing on my Kindle. Many aspects of that story in particular started floating into my brain as I read the book. A bit of friendly advise. <b>Spend less time attempting to correct people on what you feel is and isn't Lovecraftian, and perhaps spend more time interacting positively with your fellow game fans.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What? I wasn't saying Lovecraft had to. I was saying there are other authors that write about doom and horror, and yet it seems odd to me that only ever Lovecraft comes up.<br /> <br /> Since when is correcting people or trying to get them to see another perspective of a much-used trope unfriendly interaction? I'm sorry if I came across as a jerk either of those posts; I only had it out for another poster, and that's because every other one of <i>their</i> posts I read is always condescending to another poster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:31:15-08:00","id":306136,"title":"","content":"I caved and bought the book. It's incredible. I have no idea what's going on. Also; this is definitely the best art in nWoD thusfar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:44:49-08:00","id":306143,"title":"","content":"Read the book a 3rd time. The more I read, the more I fall in love with those Dark Stars. It's addictive. I probably have said it, but I will say it again, I absolutely LOVE Mummy backstory and cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:45:39-08:00","id":306144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306136#post306136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I caved and bought the book. It's incredible. I have no idea what's going on. Also; this is definitely the best art in nWoD thusfar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love all the art in Mummy, but the stuff in this book was exceptional. I loved comparing the full page artwork to some of the corresponding, sketches in the Temakh sections. Great stuff. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T14:50:03-08:00","id":306146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306144#post306144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love all the art in Mummy, but the stuff in this book was exceptional. I loved comparing the full page artwork to some of the corresponding, sketches in the Temakh sections. Great stuff.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would really like to know the name of the guy who did The Poet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T15:36:53-08:00","id":306173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306124#post306124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not gonna happen. By rights, the souls of those seven guildmasters should have been obliviated; what they got instead was the life of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Now they're stuck.<br /> <br /> C.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Never stated that those goals were actually achievable, just that they were there.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Deceived, I see the temakh intellectually stunted. They have the infinity ahead of them and behind but yet do not grow. They focus on the Judges, Iram, and the like, but purely on instinctual vengeance, or attempting to farm artists like some cattle animals. All this is half remembered instinct, the firing synapses of a corpse long dead. Looking at them, I see no real long term projects beyond simply attempting to attack the Judges in a rather childish way (someone pushed you out of a sandbox so your solution is to burn the whole playground.)<br /> <br /> Hell, if they can't even strive to be free of mortal coils, then what hope is there for them to actually stand in Duat?<br /> <br /> Which I think would be the true tragedy for the mortals. To be stuck with a creature that no only urges you to carry on a grudge that you yourself have long let pass but to also be limited by said creature's lack of curiosity and emotional immaturity at the same time. That truly would be hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T15:41:47-08:00","id":306175,"title":"","content":"Do we know if a future release will cover the Shuankhsen in a playable context? I've seen them as profoundly sympathetic since Mummy's release (blame the Oblivion fanboy deep inside my heart) and would love to see a similar treatment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T15:48:44-08:00","id":306182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306175#post306175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if a future release will cover the Shuankhsen in a playable context? I've seen them as profoundly sympathetic since Mummy's release (blame the Oblivion fanboy deep inside my heart) and would love to see a similar treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shuanksen remind me a lot of that The Mummy(1999 film) and its sequels. Not the backstory of course, but the habit that mummy had to devour people to be whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T15:56:14-08:00","id":306187,"title":"","content":"Just making sure I'm reading this right; Azar is the potentially unwilling king of Duat, there are two different groups of 42 Judges, and Irem was physically pulled (intact!) into Duat? (Wholly unrelated; will we ever see coverage of the Shuankhsen in a playable context like the Deceived got? I think they're massively sympathetic, but that could just be the Oblivion fanboy in me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T16:16:06-08:00","id":306199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div clas