"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306418#post306418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does God need to lie?<br /> <br /> That's always a fun little idea to poke at, particularly since I like looking across the room at Coyote-As-Creator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but while I value the beauty of a half-truth as much as anyone, our Deus Est Machina doesn't really seem the type to do so when bald-faced lies require a lot less creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T22:55:14-08:00","id":306429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306424#post306424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've finally gotten to Chapter Four and yes.<br /> <br /> yesssssssss<br /> <br /> (also does the extra Ren capacity from Syllables of the Broken Word also boost the number of Affinities a Restless Star can manifest or is that not the case?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, expand on your orgasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:09:42-08:00","id":306433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306424#post306424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've finally gotten to Chapter Four and yes.<br /> <br /> yesssssssss<br /> <br /> (also does the extra Ren capacity from Syllables of the Broken Word also boost the number of Affinities a Restless Star can manifest or is that not the case?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope. You just get a bigger pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:24:53-08:00","id":306436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306429#post306429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, expand on your orgasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Among other things, Ever-Dying Name and Shadows Among Fallen Pillars have given me a striking visual for my post-apocalyptic setting, Face of Endless Lies giving <i>the entire Lost Guild </i>freaky shapeshifting magic as a basic power is music to my ears (especially in combination with Whispers to My Body), and the second half of Word is the Will's first power appeals to the contrived-scenario fan in me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:28:12-08:00","id":306438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306425#post306425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but while I value the beauty of a half-truth as much as anyone, our Deus Est Machina doesn't really seem the type to do so when bald-faced lies require a lot less creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better question to ask would be why would it care about the drama with Mummies? It's busy fixing timelines, preparing the Occult Matrix, and more. Perhaps a revelation was to move the Prophet to create a cult simply to dispose of later once a project had been completed and largely cares about more active players in the game. Mummies are on a time limit, Achieve a goal, and then return to their tombs. As powerful as they are, they're mostly in stasis, old men taking naps in their tombs. None of which helps or hampers the God Machine in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Sure, it can take on secondary goals. Goals that include discovery of Sekhem and how it interacts with the occult matrix, odd discovery of the Irem Relic, Repairing the festering holes in the time line that the Rite punched into the world, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> But none of those are it's primary operations and purpose. For every resource use to harass the Arisen, the more chaos the Unchained can create. Ongoing projects need regular Outputs, Materials need to be shipped, and Infrastructure needs to be maintained. None of that stuff really affects the Arisen other than perhaps the most casual way.<br /> <br /> As a result, the GM, if it does exist in a mummy story, is purely a background character who's influence just barely makes it's self known and most likely will be confused as rival mummy cults, plans and mechanics that other Arisen have in place, some courier from the Judges, or some weirdness that this world throws out every so often.<br /> <br /> In short, you don't need to involve the Big Man in this. He's got more important things to do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:30:54-08:00","id":306440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306187#post306187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just making sure I'm reading this right; Azar is the potentially unwilling king of Duat, there are two different groups of 42 Judges, and Irem was physically pulled (intact!) into Duat? (Wholly unrelated; will we ever see coverage of the Shuankhsen in a playable context like the Deceived got? I think they're massively sympathetic, but that could just be the Oblivion fanboy in me).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Judges of Duat are left kinda ambigious to a certain extent. Likely so that the reader and ST can make up their own mind for what fits a given Mummy game that might try and uncover any truth in regard to the matter. <br /> <br /> That being said, their is a fair bit of evidence that the Judges of Duat and the Judges that birthed the Shan'Iatu are different entities. Its mentioned for example that the Celestial Judges are residents of paradise pretty much. Basically the opposite of Duat. Likewise, they are the &quot;Judges of Life&quot; while it appears the Judges of Duat are the Judges of Death that the Shan'Iatu sought to create/become (and that Azar asked about before they chopped him up &quot;Who are the Judges of Death?&quot;). <br /> <br /> Other factors are the remoteness of the Celestial Judges as exceedingly abstract patterns of Fate that seem to dwell above even the Nameless Gods like Azar and Anpu. While the teaching of Irem had the Judges of Duat as very interested and involved in mortal lifetimes (since they had to punish transgressions) and that they were much closer to mankind then the Nameless Gods. <br /> <br /> This gets more complex and interesting when you add in that CAS has mentioned several times that the Judges of Duat are not just the ascended Shan'Iatu. Instead one might view them as an attempt by the Shan'Iatu to enter Duat and rule under Azar there. However, the end result might have been the creation of a separate group of entities by the Shan'Iatu, as effectively a by-product of them sacrificing Irem (and possibly themselves) to Ammut. In a more liner way, perhaps getting new &quot;true names&quot; changed the Shan'Iatu more then they expected and instead of becoming the same old beings in new forms they became new beings full stop. <br /> <br /> Frankly everything that happened after the Rite of Return was enacted is really still a big ???. We don't know when or were the Judges of Duat came from after the Rite, though the timeless nature of the Rite of Return makes it look like they existed before the Rite was enacted. I suspect this is something we once again will not get a hard answer too, though Dreams of Avarice might provide more insights (given that the Heretic can remember what is going on in Duat now). <br /> <br /> Also as someone pointed out, the fiction at the start of Deceived does have an unreliable narrator who seems to get several elements wrong (such as the Shan'Iatu's &quot;human&quot; gender) if what the devs have to say is any indication. So while I am sure it does paint a more complete picture then the story we got in the Corebook, I'm also pretty open to the idea that their are some purposeful errors or red-herrings again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:38:52-08:00","id":306443,"title":"","content":"All I can really say is &quot;Wow!&quot; The Deceived are not at all what I expected, and all the more awesome for it.<br /> <br /> My only problem with the book is I still really don't get what seba actually are. They're confluences of Fate that manifest as great works of art? So Beethoven's 5th is an expression of seba, say? But if a Deceived was there when Beethoven composed it, they could have &quot;sucked out&quot; the metaphysical oomph so that it would still exist, but would have no real power and probably have been forgotten?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:45:59-08:00","id":306447,"title":"","content":"It might be that they poisoned the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T00:00:42-08:00","id":306451,"title":"","content":"The basic truth of the setting, as I understand it, is that if you're a mummy - Arisen, Deceived or Shuankhsen - you're not your own free man. Someone (who that someone is differs between factions) is playing puppetmaster and using you as a slave/tool/soldier in its war. And we're talking about a war that is most likely significantly older than 6000 years, and that has most likely lost all meaning in the context of the present time. The tragedy of the setting is that mummies are slaves; to causes that have died millenia ago. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T00:29:14-08:00","id":306458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306360#post306360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hum by resembling a Shuankhsen I mean he devours people like they do. And he got more powerful not less, like Shuanksen do, when they devour mortals they replenish their Pillar Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Shuankhsen start at Sekhem 3, though. They're not exactly calling down meteors<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306394#post306394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. If I did anything clever there, it was making sure that the concept could work either way. And for Imhotep as presented, I think it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...maybe I'm just overly tired. Imhotep could be justified as any type of the three, yeah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T00:49:51-08:00","id":306461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306443#post306443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can really say is &quot;Wow!&quot; The Deceived are not at all what I expected, and all the more awesome for it.<br /> <br /> My only problem with the book is I still really don't get what seba actually are. They're confluences of Fate that manifest as great works of art? So Beethoven's 5th is an expression of seba, say? But if a Deceived was there when Beethoven composed it, they could have &quot;sucked out&quot; the metaphysical oomph so that it would still exist, but would have no real power and probably have been forgotten?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad we wowed you. Seba are patterns of numinous Sekhem that are created sometimes by masterful art and other times by the Sekhem of the cosmos itself. You attach them to your soul and they become part of you, giving you the curse and power associated with them. Think of them as post-it notes stuck onto your true name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T03:09:29-08:00","id":306505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306424#post306424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've finally gotten to Chapter Four and yes.<br /> <br /> yesssssssss<br /> <br /> (also does the extra Ren capacity from Syllables of the Broken Word also boost the number of Affinities a Restless Star can manifest or is that not the case?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feels strangely gleeful at this. I try not to be THAT GUY who gets a new book and immediately goes, &quot;Ohhh lets check out the cool new powers!&quot;.....but I do. But strictly in the sense of what are mechanics that really play well to how you want to tell a story of these creepy mummies. They really hit it out of the park I think on what toys the Deceived can play with that really helps setting up either making an npc feel like a good horror story boogieman but make a player feel like &quot;Yeah that's what I'm playing.&quot; and really feel like the game is hitting the right tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T03:15:32-08:00","id":306507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306440#post306440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Judges of Duat are left kinda ambigious to a certain extent. Likely so that the reader and ST can make up their own mind for what fits a given Mummy game that might try and uncover any truth in regard to the matter.<br /> <br /> That being said, their is a fair bit of evidence that the Judges of Duat and the Judges that birthed the Shan'Iatu are different entities. Its mentioned for example that the Celestial Judges are residents of paradise pretty much. Basically the opposite of Duat. Likewise, they are the &quot;Judges of Life&quot; while it appears the Judges of Duat are the Judges of Death that the Shan'Iatu sought to create/become (and that Azar asked about before they chopped him up &quot;Who are the Judges of Death?&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost wonder if either A. It was all some set up of Ammut to get them into Duat, though I sort of doubt that as I don't figure her for having much actual power in Duat. But more a long what you sad earlier, that perhaps the changing of their True Names effectively made them new beings though that means still wondering why there are 42 still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306440#post306440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gets more complex and interesting when you add in that CAS has mentioned several times that the Judges of Duat are not just the ascended Shan'Iatu. Instead one might view them as an attempt by the Shan'Iatu to enter Duat and rule under Azar there. However, the end result might have been the creation of a separate group of entities by the Shan'Iatu, as effectively a by-product of them sacrificing Irem (and possibly themselves) to Ammut. In a more liner way, perhaps getting new &quot;true names&quot; changed the Shan'Iatu more then they expected and instead of becoming the same old beings in new forms they became new beings full stop.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I didn't expect this at first, given the way the game keeps referencing back to Fate and how much we learned about Nomenclature and apparently what they could do then. It would be true in an &quot;Obi Wan&quot; sort of way that while technically the Judges of Duat are the Shan'iatu they are completely new beings with the changes to their True Names. But again the 42 thing bugs me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306440#post306440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly everything that happened after the Rite of Return was enacted is really still a big ???. We don't know when or were the Judges of Duat came from after the Rite, though the timeless nature of the Rite of Return makes it look like they existed before the Rite was enacted. I suspect this is something we once again will not get a hard answer too, though Dreams of Avarice might provide more insights (given that the Heretic can remember what is going on in Duat now).<br /> <br /> Also as someone pointed out, the fiction at the start of Deceived does have an unreliable narrator who seems to get several elements wrong (such as the Shan'Iatu's &quot;human&quot; gender) if what the devs have to say is any indication. So while I am sure it does paint a more complete picture then the story we got in the Corebook, I'm also pretty open to the idea that their are some purposeful errors or red-herrings again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes me wonder do they mean to reveal like what the narrator of Deceived would have us believe, that the Shan'iatu wanted to be Gods still over Duat and Irem so they could enjoy the human pleasures they took up. Or something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-08-2014, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T03:46:34-08:00","id":306514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306507#post306507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I didn't expect this at first, given the way the game keeps referencing back to Fate and how much we learned about Nomenclature and apparently what they could do then. It would be true in an &quot;Obi Wan&quot; sort of way that while technically the Judges of Duat are the Shan'iatu they are completely new beings with the changes to their True Names. But again the 42 thing bugs me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the numbers thing, it's also odd that the Judges of Duat pick their servants by Decree. If they really were the Shan'iatu, you'd think they'd go for Mummies from particular Guilds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306458#post306458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Shuankhsen start at Sekhem 3, though. They're not exactly calling down meteors</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, Sekhem 3 is enough to call down meteors. You just need to do it one at a time.<br /> <br /> The giant sandstorm is a bit more difficult to justify though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T09:05:05-08:00","id":306694,"title":"","content":"Who wrote The Dancer? My absolute favorite among the temakh, by far. (I'll likely be using BotD as the framework for a Geist chronicle, oddly enough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T10:55:28-08:00","id":306802,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Shan'iatu pulled the Judges of Life into Duat and/or merged with them. Maybe they assigned their True Names to those Judges, who previously had been somewhat vague and unknowable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T10:59:14-08:00","id":306804,"title":"","content":"The fact that there are 42 Judges (regardless of if you believe in a single set or two different sets) does pretty much make it seem like the Shan'Iatu did not manage to pull off their &quot;enter Duat as Gods&quot; thing. As we know for a fact 7 of them are still stuck on Earth inside the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm of the idea that Ammut pulled a fast one on the Shan'Iatu. Their Rite of Return did not elevate them it just dropped them into her lap. However, since magic has to do &quot;something&quot; when it enacted (its an active force after all and a sacrifice was made) she kinda &quot;fulfilled&quot; her end of the bargain and the Judges are the result. Hence because the Judges deal with her has a place in Duat for all 42 of them, 42 Judges popped up. The timeless nature of the Rite made it so that from a mortal point of view the Judges had always been in Duat, but no one save Anpu and Ammut can likely realize that they only showed up after Irems fall. <br /> <br /> Basically, I'm certain (in no small part thanks to CAS's comments on this topic) that the Judges are distinct from the Shan'Iatu and not a continuation of them in Duat. What I'm not exactly sure on is what happened to the other 35 Shan'Iatu once the Rite of Return was enacted. Either that little fact is going to be forever left &quot;up to the ST&quot; or I think Dreams might detail it. Time will tell. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who wrote The Dancer? My absolute favorite among the temakh, by far. </div> </div> </div>I too have a soft spot for the Dancer. In so far as his &quot;art&quot;/seba is <i>trances</i> which is the only type of seba I really have any experience with myself. I'm not a dancer (two left feet) but I've done martial arts for years and experienced &quot;no-mind&quot; like states while practicing forms or stances before. <br /> <br /> Apart from him, I like the Philosopher, as I always have time for nihilistic villains that are well executed and hypocritical characters. Also have more then a few friends who did Philosophy degrees and often fly into rages when they can't debunk and argument they don't like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Poet is kinda cool as well. Though I like is aspect of Storyteller (for obvious reasons) far more then the idea of his relation to actual Poetry. <br /> <br /> The Musician and Singer I can't really fully appreciate I feel having no musical talent myself. The Keeper is the hardest for me to wrap my head around. Revelation is after all, hard to grasp unless you've undergone it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T11:13:26-08:00","id":306812,"title":"","content":"I've felt moments of each of these guys seba throughout my life.<br /> <br /> Really, I'd play the Deceived for no other reason than how intimately I understand what they seek and what they've lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:44:57-08:00","id":306886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306694#post306694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wrote The Dancer? My absolute favorite among the temakh, by far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hiya. I polished all the temakhs, made them fit into the same framework and voice, but I assigned the Dancer to George. He and Khaldoun (who wrote the Keeper) were my go-to guys once I knew what I wanted to do with <i>Belial's Brood</i>, and I wanted to get the proverbial band back together for this one.<br /> <br /> Being a musician and singer myself, of course I held those in reserve for my own pen.<br /> <br /> C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:57:42-08:00","id":306891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306804#post306804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Poet is kinda cool as well. Though I like is aspect of Storyteller (for obvious reasons) far more then the idea of his relation to actual Poetry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psst: &quot;actual poetry&quot; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narrative_poetry\" target=\"_blank\">is not a distinct thing from storytelling in this sense.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-08-2014, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T14:55:58-08:00","id":306937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306891#post306891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psst: &quot;actual poetry&quot; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narrative_poetry\" target=\"_blank\">is not a distinct thing from storytelling in this sense.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Urrggghhh...You know when you realize that you've got a limited image of something in your head. Then someone points out that limited image and you think/say:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah of course like (example, example, example), man how could I not include those things together duh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there a word for that feeling. Because its what i'm overwhelmed by at current. <br /> <br /> P.s. Is it just me or do the Deceived lack any supernatural means of uncovering true names?<br /> <br /> I'm just about half way through the Seba section of Chapter Four. So all the talk about True Names and such is mentioned earlier in the chapter. After looking through all the Affinities and Utterances I noticed the Deceived don't have any that actually &quot;show&quot; a persons/items true name to them. While the Scribes Level 5 Guild Affinity from Guildhalls does which seem weird to me. Have a missed something here or is it the case that they have to do a load of occult research like anyone else to figure out a true name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T18:39:46-08:00","id":307059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306804#post306804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that there are 42 Judges (regardless of if you believe in a single set or two different sets) does pretty much make it seem like the Shan'Iatu did not manage to pull off their &quot;enter Duat as Gods&quot; thing. As we know for a fact 7 of them are still stuck on Earth inside the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm of the idea that Ammut pulled a fast one on the Shan'Iatu. Their Rite of Return did not elevate them it just dropped them into her lap. However, since magic has to do &quot;something&quot; when it enacted (its an active force after all and a sacrifice was made) she kinda &quot;fulfilled&quot; her end of the bargain and the Judges are the result. Hence because the Judges deal with her has a place in Duat for all 42 of them, 42 Judges popped up. The timeless nature of the Rite made it so that from a mortal point of view the Judges had always been in Duat, but no one save Anpu and Ammut can likely realize that they only showed up after Irems fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure that this is the case. The opening chapter states that souls would appear in Duat before the Judges, to be assessed in accordance with the Law and carried on to Duat if they proved worthy. This was before Irem was even founded. To me, it sounds like the Judges of Life dwelt in A'aru, but occasionally nipped down to Duat to proffer judgement upon the living. As written, it's entirely possible that the original 42 Judges that existed before the Shan'iatu are the same Judges the Arisen serve.<br /> <br /> I agree that the fate of the other Shan'iatu was certainly not to become the Judges. Between the number discrepancy and the fact that the Judges chose their servants based on Decree, not Guild, it offers precious few connections between the two in its current state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T18:52:54-08:00","id":307079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306937#post306937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Urrggghhh...You know when you realize that you've got a limited image of something in your head. Then someone points out that limited image and you think/say:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah of course like (example, example, example), man how could I not include those things together duh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is there a word for that feeling. Because its what i'm overwhelmed by at current.<br /> <br /> P.s. Is it just me or do the Deceived lack any supernatural means of uncovering true names?<br /> <br /> I'm just about half way through the Seba section of Chapter Four. So all the talk about True Names and such is mentioned earlier in the chapter. After looking through all the Affinities and Utterances I noticed the Deceived don't have any that actually &quot;show&quot; a persons/items true name to them. While the Scribes Level 5 Guild Affinity from Guildhalls does which seem weird to me. Have a missed something here or is it the case that they have to do a load of occult research like anyone else to figure out a true name?</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I got from both Mummy and Mage is that getting True Names is far more research, occult knowledge, insight into the entity,etc research work rather than a matter of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T19:32:45-08:00","id":307097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307079#post307079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The impression I got from both Mummy and Mage is that getting True Names is far more research, occult knowledge, insight into the entity,etc research work rather than a matter of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be worth considering a name versus a True Name. Pretty sure Mage didn't actually reference True Names until like, Imperial Mysteries. All you need is someone's regular name for sympathetic magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T20:19:27-08:00","id":307108,"title":"","content":"Could someone make a collage of all the temakh art? I'd love to see them all in one image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T20:30:42-08:00","id":307111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307097#post307097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might be worth considering a name versus a True Name. Pretty sure Mage didn't actually reference True Names until like, Imperial Mysteries. All you need is someone's regular name for sympathetic magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Um yeah I wasn't talking about sympathetic magic directly. But I get what you are saying. The impression I got was that True Names require a lot of delicate insight into something if you wanted to get it in situations brute magical strength wouldn't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T23:45:23-08:00","id":307212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307111#post307111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um yeah I wasn't talking about sympathetic magic directly. But I get what you are saying. The impression I got was that True Names require a lot of delicate insight into something if you wanted to get it in situations brute magical strength wouldn't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably. It'd be cool if we could get some better idea of what a True Name is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T00:49:36-08:00","id":307248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307212#post307212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be cool if we could get some better idea of what a True Name is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Your wish is my command. Folks will have everything they need to run the heck out of some Deceived in their <b>Mummy</b> chronicles, including True Name material.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned.<br /> <br /> C.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T01:57:25-08:00","id":307271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307079#post307079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The impression I got from both Mummy and Mage is that getting True Names is far more research, occult knowledge, insight into the entity,etc research work rather than a matter of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that 9 times out of 10 research, questing and all that should be a thing in a game to learn a beings True Name. In a mortals game involving Demons (Inferno type) having to track down all the literature and dodgy cults to find out the True Name of the demon troubling your loved ones. In a Mage game the whole investigation thing fits very nicely with the &quot;uncover the mysteries of the world&quot; theme that Mage has going for it.<br /> <br /> Mummy's a different creature I feel though. Considering that Mummy's already set the president for being able to use Iremite/Arisen magic to find True Names in Guildhalls of the Deathless. As I mentioned in my previous posts the Scribes Level 5 Guild Affinity &quot;Erudite Bastion of Perfection&quot; (Guildhalls of the Deathless p.111) allows them to piece together the True Name of objects and entities. <br /> <br /> At current, the Deceived, who are supposed to be masters of Name Magic have no innate or even optional magical method of doing the same thing a Scribe Guildmaster can do. This just feels kinda...off to me. A load of their abilities mention IF you have a targets True Name (some just need any name and that's kinda cool), but at current the Deceived have to go through the same basically &quot;mortal&quot; process of occult research and &quot;insight&quot; as everyone else. Once again, this just feels kinda...weird in regard to the master of name magic. <br /> <br /> Hopefully the update CAS mentioned in his last post will go into this a bit more (namely what is a true name, how to get hold of one and how the Deceived are better at doing so then everyone else). I'm hoping its an addenda to Book of the Deceived (like the mirage rules added to DC) and not material in a later book in the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T05:03:27-08:00","id":307332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307271#post307271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully the update CAS mentioned in his last post will go into this a bit more (namely what is a true name, how to get hold of one and how the Deceived are better at doing so then everyone else). I'm hoping its an addenda to Book of the Deceived (like the mirage rules added to DC) and not material in a later book in the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is a little out of place but nothing that GM fiat can't handle. But for Deceived PCs? Hm.<br /> <br /> Remember, too, the Deceived's temakh aren't as powerful as they used to be. They look at modern Utterances with disdain and think they're child's play compared to what they used to be able to do. There's still a lot of name magic in the book. Still, I agree with you. Luckily the ball's already rolling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T05:23:00-08:00","id":307340,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about the Deceived in context as NPC's mainly, as while I find them very engaging and would love to play one, I'm not sure they are my local player groups cup of tea for play. Hence my interesting how good they are at getting hold of true names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":".  Found the Answer to my original question concerning Agg damage. 11-09-2014, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T09:28:40-08:00","id":307494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306886#post306886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hiya. I polished all the temakhs, made them fit into the same framework and voice, but I assigned the Dancer to George. He and Khaldoun (who wrote the Keeper) were my go-to guys once I knew what I wanted to do with <i>Belial's Brood</i>, and I wanted to get the proverbial band back together for this one.<br /> <br /> Being a musician and singer myself, of course I held those in reserve for my own pen.<br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>CAS I forgot or I didn't remember that you were also involved in Belial's Brood. It was one of the best material I've read for Vampire. You and your team really have a knack to write top-class material for the darkests bits of the WOD. Hope to see more of it in the future, in any gameline.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T09:37:19-08:00","id":307497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307332#post307332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it is a little out of place but nothing that GM fiat can't handle. But for Deceived PCs? Hm.<br /> <br /> Remember, too, the Deceived's temakh aren't as powerful as they used to be. They look at modern Utterances with disdain and think they're child's play compared to what they used to be able to do. There's still a lot of name magic in the book. Still, I agree with you. Luckily the ball's already rolling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They are much better at exploring True Names, that's their magic, but yes a bit about uncovering them would have been nice too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:45:15-08:00","id":307831,"title":"","content":"BotD repeatedly mentions that the Akhem-Urtu view the Sesha-Hebsu as kin, but there's surprisingly little on their thoughts regarding the Tef-Aabhi and that confuses me. Wouldn't artists feel intense kinship with the masons? Architecture is an art form in of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:59:53-08:00","id":307848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307497#post307497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are much better at exploring True Names, that's their magic, but yes a bit about uncovering them would have been nice too.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the fluff yes, they are supposed to be the only people who have any proper grasp of True Name magic. <br /> <br /> Mechanically at current (as the errataed version might change this from what CAS seems to be hinting at) they are absolutely no better then anyone else at finding out True Names.<br /> <br /> The other issue I've noticed is their ability to stay hidden and &quot;a myth&quot; from the Arisen. <br /> <br /> Their level 1 Guild Affinity makes them pretty much perfect disguise artists from mundane observation (as does one of their Soul Affinities). Their level 2 Guild Affinity protects them from most forms of Mummy specific magical sights (the Soul Sight affinity in particular). The general fact they have &quot;super&quot; Engima as a extra merit thingy is pretty good for getting rid of any mundane traces they leave and can stack with several Affinities that let them hide mundane evidence of their existence very well. <br /> <br /> Thing is, they don't have any obvious protection from Godsight, an Affinity that a fair few Arisen have, indeed its mentioned that their level 1 Guild Affinity is pierced by Godsight. The shape-shifting Soul Affinity makes no mention of it, but its basically a passive magic effect on them all the time, exactly the sort of thing Godsight can see (though in this case the Deceived's true form would not be revealed only that they had a shape-shifting power active). The level 2 Guild Affinity does not apply. <br /> <br /> They almost certainly cause a -5 to the WIts+Occult roll Godsight grants to spot supernatural creatures/active magics I would imagine due to their rarity and their &quot;myth&quot; status. Other then that Enigma might add another -5 only if they were in a crowd when it was active. Even then the Arisen could spend a Willpower for extra dice and all he/she needs is 1 success. Given how good Godsight is at identifying magic and supernatural creatures, this would mean an Arisen would pretty much (with a more evocative description in game) get the answer from the ST of &quot;a Deceived&quot; if they got a success.<br /> <br /> Once again, maybe something the errata will deal with. Pretty easy to fix by removing Godsights ability to pierce the Level 1 Guild Affinity. Or maybe some text can be added to the Level 2 Guild Affinity to say it also negates general magic sights like Godsight's ability to detect the Deceived as anything other then an Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:57:17-08:00","id":307916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307831#post307831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BotD repeatedly mentions that the Akhem-Urtu view the Sesha-Hebsu as kin, but there's surprisingly little on their thoughts regarding the Tef-Aabhi and that confuses me. Wouldn't artists feel intense kinship with the masons? Architecture is an art form in of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're putting form before function. The Arisen collect <i>tools</i>. The relics of the Five aren't spontaneously/providentially-generated magical if-then statements given substance for roughly the same reason that we don't reasonably expect a refined working computer to just fall out of the sky <i>ex nihilo</i>. The seba <i>have</i> no form, owing to their being fortuitous convergences of transcendent principles that evoke magic capable of <i>subverting causality</i>.<br /> <br /> The effigies of the Father of Idols have magic that relates to the specific properties of those relics - meanwhile, only two types of non-cosmic seba aren't named for obvious <i>byproducts</i> of artistic endeavor (and the remainder includes one that derives its English name from a word meaning &quot;prayer&quot;), and &quot;artistic seba that aren't claimed disperse into the cosmic background glow and re-manifest somewhere else with no particular link to their genesis,&quot; along with the existence of cosmic seba, would seem to indicate that the masons' work is rather <i>lesser</i>, to the temakh's perspective.<br /> <br /> (There's also that whole &quot;the Masons want to <i>make a new Irem</i>&quot; thing from Guildhalls that's a bit of a dealbreaker for the folks who want to commit <i>damnatio memoriae</i> on the progenitor of modern civilization.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-10-2014, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:59:26-08:00","id":308009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=307848#post307848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other issue I've noticed is their ability to stay hidden and &quot;a myth&quot; from the Arisen.<br /> <br /> Their level 1 Guild Affinity makes them pretty much perfect disguise artists from mundane observation (as does one of their Soul Affinities). Their level 2 Guild Affinity protects them from most forms of Mummy specific magical sights (the Soul Sight affinity in particular). The general fact they have &quot;super&quot; Engima as a extra merit thingy is pretty good for getting rid of any mundane traces they leave and can stack with several Affinities that let them hide mundane evidence of their existence very well.<br /> <br /> Thing is, they don't have any obvious protection from Godsight, an Affinity that a fair few Arisen have, indeed its mentioned that their level 1 Guild Affinity is pierced by Godsight. The shape-shifting Soul Affinity makes no mention of it, but its basically a passive magic effect on them all the time, exactly the sort of thing Godsight can see (though in this case the Deceived's true form would not be revealed only that they had a shape-shifting power active). The level 2 Guild Affinity does not apply.<br /> <br /> They almost certainly cause a -5 to the WIts+Occult roll Godsight grants to spot supernatural creatures/active magics I would imagine due to their rarity and their &quot;myth&quot; status. Other then that Enigma might add another -5 only if they were in a crowd when it was active. Even then the Arisen could spend a Willpower for extra dice and all he/she needs is 1 success. Given how good Godsight is at identifying magic and supernatural creatures, this would mean an Arisen would pretty much (with a more evocative description in game) get the answer from the ST of &quot;a Deceived&quot; if they got a success.<br /> <br /> Once again, maybe something the errata will deal with. Pretty easy to fix by removing Godsights ability to pierce the Level 1 Guild Affinity. Or maybe some text can be added to the Level 2 Guild Affinity to say it also negates general magic sights like Godsight's ability to detect the Deceived as anything other then an Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Godsight doesn't strike me as being particularly common, though. The followers of Uatch-Rekhet are guaranteed to have it, as are a fifth of Usekh-Nemtet's followers. Given how many Affinities there are, and that Mummies start with 2-3 non-Guild Affinities, I can't see it being particularly likely that anyone outside of those two will have the Affinity. But let's be generous and assume that one in twenty Arisen do.<br /> <br /> So we couple scarcity with two other important elements. The first is Memory, wherein a Mummy that actually encounters and knows they encountered a Deceived will inevitably forget the encounter. Supporting evidence, like written documents and first-hand accounts of witnesses, are not impossible to destroy. The second is that the Deceived seem to tend towards &quot;from the shadows&quot; kind of plots rather than direct confrontations, severely limiting exposure.<br /> <br /> With all this, it's not surprising that the Deceived are little more than rumours, at least to me. Godsight, if anything, just provides an explanation for why there even are rumours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T07:48:14-08:00","id":308211,"title":"","content":"To my recollection, Mummies have few 'shape-shifting' powers that really disguise them or turn them into something subtle, like an animal. Any appearance alterations are usually dramatic, Epic, and oozing with Sybaris. I could be wrong here, but do Mummies really have any reason to use Godsight on every Mummy they encounter? How many of us here have run or are running a campaign with a PC doing that to NPC Mummies?<br /> <br /> I know that's not necessarily the best answer, but I'm just saying that, in-universe, I'm not sure the Arisen have much reason to be suspicious in the same way Vampires, Changelings, or Mages have to be. If they knew the Deceived existed then they would, but they don't...so.<br /> <br /> Finally, so what if they see through the illusion of that Affinity? Then they see a horrible monster that they're just going to, again in-universe, assume is a Shuankhsen then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:04:59-08:00","id":308375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=308211#post308211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could be wrong here, but do Mummies really have any reason to use Godsight on every Mummy they encounter? How many of us here have run or are running a campaign with a PC doing that to NPC Mummies?</div> </div> </div> </div>The campaign I ran had a PC with Godsight, he used it a lot. Like every time something new mystically happened. It made doing occult mystery plot really difficult in my experience.<br /> <br /> I openly admit though, the Godsight thing is more a personal niggle on my part, due to previous experiences. Its not a major thing that I feel breaks the verisimilitude of the setting or anything. If it stays as it is I'm not going to feel like the Deceived have been short changed or anything, or that they can't function as their fluff suggests. <br /> <br /> The True Name issue does bug me something awful though. From other comments on a few threads here is seems other people are having issues with it to. Though considering CAS and Nephilpal have both mentioned that more info on True Names and how the Deceived interact with them (hopefully giving them a way of finding them out easier then just mundane research like mortal have to resort too) is coming (hopefully in the addenda'd pdf of Book of the Deceived) I'm not too worried about this point either really. <br /> <br /> Though recently (as in yesterday) my local player group (this is about 10 different people split into three different groups) pretty much all said they would never run or play in a Mummy game as the game stands at current. Basically, they've said they are going to wait until Mummy Second Ed around 2017 before trying the game again. So I'm pretty much reading the Mummy books for personal interest and fluff now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:59:48-08:00","id":308419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=308375#post308375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The campaign I ran had a PC with Godsight, he used it a lot. Like every time something new mystically happened. It made doing occult mystery plot really difficult in my experience.<br /> <br /> I openly admit though, the Godsight thing is more a personal niggle on my part, due to previous experiences. Its not a major thing that I feel breaks the verisimilitude of the setting or anything. If it stays as it is I'm not going to feel like the Deceived have been short changed or anything, or that they can't function as their fluff suggests.<br /> <br /> The True Name issue does bug me something awful though. From other comments on a few threads here is seems other people are having issues with it to. Though considering CAS and Nephilpal have both mentioned that more info on True Names and how the Deceived interact with them (hopefully giving them a way of finding them out easier then just mundane research like mortal have to resort too) is coming (hopefully in the addenda'd pdf of Book of the Deceived) I'm not too worried about this point either really.<br /> <br /> Though recently (as in yesterday) my local player group (this is about 10 different people split into three different groups) pretty much all said they would never run or play in a Mummy game as the game stands at current. Basically, they've said they are going to wait until Mummy Second Ed around 2017 before trying the game again. So I'm pretty much reading the Mummy books for personal interest and fluff now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been tough to find a group to play Mummy here in Rio as well. Or NWOD for that matter. Heck even CWOD can be difficult at times. But Mummy books are more than worth just by the fluff. Been reading Guildhalls and the Core again on my free time. Boy how this game have grow a lot!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T12:29:30-08:00","id":308447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=306507#post306507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I almost wonder if either A. It was all some set up of Ammut to get them into Duat, though I sort of doubt that as I don't figure her for having much actual power in Duat. But more a long what you sad earlier, that perhaps the changing of their True Names effectively made them new beings though that means still wondering why there are 42 still.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While I didn't expect this at first, given the way the game keeps referencing back to Fate and how much we learned about Nomenclature and apparently what they could do then. It would be true in an &quot;Obi Wan&quot; sort of way that while technically the Judges of Duat are the Shan'iatu they are completely new beings with the changes to their True Names. But again the 42 thing bugs me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder do they mean to reveal like what the narrator of Deceived would have us believe, that the Shan'iatu wanted to be Gods still over Duat and Irem so they could enjoy the human pleasures they took up. Or something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 42 Judges may or may not be the Shan'iatu but it seens to be very very likely that they aren't the Judges that created them in the first place. They are the Judges of Death, and seens extremently dependent on the Sekhem gathered by the Arisen.<br /> Another thing I wanted to know is what the relationship the &quot;original&quot; Judges have to Fate, if its the Law that was referenced time and time again at the beginning of Chapter One.<br /> One thing about Fate we are certain, it doesn't want Seba to fall in the hands of the Judges, so it kinds of gives credence that whatever the Judges of Death may be, they don't seen be the original Judges at all. I suspect one of Fate's objectives is to guide the Arisen to Apotheosis as a way to avoid the relics to fall into Duat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T14:54:50-08:00","id":308529,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading<br /> <br /> It's just me or the Shan'Iatu were a special kind of douchebags? And can give a run to Mages in the Hubris category<br /> <br /> The only thing that bugs me is their total lack of devotion to their duty. According to chapter 1 they battled the Devourer exactly once and were very suceptible to corruption. Their gods seems also very passive towards the same corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","user":"ganonso","date":". 11-10-2014, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:20:44-08:00","id":308549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=308529#post308529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished reading<br /> <br /> It's just me or the Shan'Iatu were a special kind of douchebags? And can give a run to Mages in the Hubris category<br /> <br /> The only thing that bugs me is their total lack of devotion to their duty. According to chapter 1 they battled the Devourer exactly once and were very suceptible to corruption. Their gods seems also very passive towards the same corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the same too. For me they had a very nice deal from the Judges, but felt so entitled that they wanted basically to have it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:25:58-08:00","id":308552,"title":"","content":"Oh, lest I forget: the commentary on the nature of the Rite lends a new degree of understanding to this old quote from Greg Stolze:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">&quot;Do you want to be Good Soldier Hans and sacrifice yourself for the Greater Good? (Well, the Greater SOMETHING anyhow.) <b>Or do you want to be your own man at the cost of flipping the bird to undying powers that BROKE TIME?</b>&quot;</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:26:38-08:00","id":308553,"title":"","content":"I think the Shan'iatu clearly outstripped every mage there is(maybe not those that were).<br /> <br /> As for their failure to battle Ammut, eh. These sorts of narratives exist all over in mythology. Besides, when talking to a Kali-meets-Lucifer figure, one expects to get severely distracted from what one was doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T17:21:48-08:00","id":308657,"title":"","content":"Also they had been wounded and that corruption infected them like spiritual sepsis. It's not like they fell to darkness with the barest nudge like Anakin in Episode 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T22:37:42-08:00","id":308863,"title":"","content":"...and technically that one 'battle? They won that. Ammut didn't send anymore magic armies after them. She just talked to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T22:41:34-08:00","id":308865,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I would be quite interested in a future supplement exploring those places of corruption and the Amkhat Ammut spawned herself. The brief description of the latter makes it sound quite different from normal Amkhata. Capable of inflicting something like Bane Affinities, for one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T22:47:28-08:00","id":308867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=308529#post308529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished reading<br /> <br /> It's just me or the Shan'Iatu were a special kind of douchebags? And can give a run to Mages in the Hubris category<br /> <br /> The only thing that bugs me is their total lack of devotion to their duty. According to chapter 1 they battled the Devourer exactly once and were very suceptible to corruption. Their gods seems also very passive towards the same corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they did almost exactly what they were supposed to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T23:01:54-08:00","id":308872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=308867#post308867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, they did almost exactly what they were supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>White mutinies the world over hinge on that &quot;almost,&quot; don't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T03:04:09-08:00","id":308913,"title":"","content":"Huh? Color me confused <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T03:17:41-08:00","id":308916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=308913#post308913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? Color me confused <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I guess they did build the Nameless Empire like the Judges wanted, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T08:54:20-08:00","id":309169,"title":"","content":"The Empire was <i>nowhere</i> in their contract.<br /> <br /> But teaching what they knew was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:35:13-08:00","id":309231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=309169#post309169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Empire was <i>nowhere</i> in their contract.<br /> <br /> But teaching what they knew was.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I guess the suffering they brought wasn't really necessary as well. Really they rationale for revenge was: poor us, the Judges denied us paradise(never mind that they gave us immense powers and made us immortal, never mind that we could rule as Gods among man, because we can't go to Paradise the Judges are cruel so we must be cruel)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:37:14-08:00","id":309233,"title":"","content":"Really Shan'iatu are the most entitled S.O.Bs that the WOD ever had. So delicious arrogants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 11-11-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:51:14-08:00","id":309242,"title":"","content":"Well, let's be fair here. We don't know what Azar and the Judges really had in mind.<br /> <br /> Imagine you knew of-were taught about the most wonderful and exquisite place, by people you felt close to, people you adored and/or respected.<br /> <br /> Imagine you got it in your head that you would never be allowed into that place.<br /> <br /> Imagine the people you adore and respected told you your job was to prepare people for that place.<br /> <br /> Imagine how pissed <i>you'd</i> be.<br /> <br /> While this is an overly simple version of what's going on(<i>really</i> bluntly overly simple), notice that there's a disconnect in the second sentence.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the Shan'iatu are justified-far from it. But I think their sins come from a place most people will have confronted at least once, and I think their choices reflect their ironic naivete-for let's be fair again, for knowing as much as they did, as vastly powerful and knowledgeable as they were, they still seemed rather young in some sense of the word when they first experienced things.<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu are bastards, all right-but somehow, despite everything,they manage to be a remarkably human kind of bastard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T16:22:49-08:00","id":309565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=309242#post309242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shan'iatu are bastards, all right--but somehow, despite everything, they manage to be a remarkably human kind of bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I &quot;Liked&quot; your post, but this line deserves a double-up on that sentiment, methinks.<br /> <br /> Like-idy Like Like.<br /> <br /> C.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T16:31:08-08:00","id":309571,"title":"","content":"Can someone get me one of those anime faces where the person is blushing hardcore but looks seriously pleased? I need one.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T17:32:00-08:00","id":309660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=304832#post304832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, am I the only one that got a big idiot grin when the last bit about the Heretic was mentioned? Considering that Mummy is a pretty dark game, its nice to have a &quot;big good&quot; in the background. Plus his quest for Apotheosis and the results of him achieving it seem to be far more far reaching then I maybe first envisioned &quot;he's an artist&quot; indeed. Honestly, he's starting to get up to Count F***ing Dracula and Verney levels of cannon NPC popularity for me now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am, for the first time ever in the nWoD, lost. Who's Verney?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T17:36:36-08:00","id":309664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=309660#post309660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am, for the first time ever in the nWoD, lost. Who's Verney?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Frankenstein's Monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T18:04:07-08:00","id":309685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=309664#post309664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankenstein's Monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>AKA the biggest badass the living World of Darkness knows. When Count F***ing Dracula walks into town,everyone pisses their pants. When Verney walks into town, Count F***ing Dracula pisses his pants.<br /> <br /> Twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T18:04:38-08:00","id":309686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=309242#post309242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Shan'iatu are bastards, all right-but somehow, despite everything,they manage to be a remarkably human kind of bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they are very human bastards. I love how much of a bastards they are. Magnificent bastards.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T10:03:44-08:00","id":310365,"title":"","content":"You know what I keep coming back to? The seba that lets you fully purge a person of all ailments and diseases, including old age. Are you 102, riddled with cancer, and on your deathbed? Not any more. Now you're hale, healthy, and in your prime. What an incredible McGuffin that is; very, very powerful people would kill for it. And it's only a rank 3 seba. Wow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T10:36:25-08:00","id":310383,"title":"","content":"So already re-read all the Mummy books except for D.C after I read Deceived and I have to ask... how soon is too soon to ask for Sothis?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T12:17:54-08:00","id":310429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310365#post310365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I keep coming back to? The seba that lets you fully purge a person of all ailments and diseases, including old age. Are you 102, riddled with cancer, and on your deathbed? Not any more. Now you're hale, healthy, and in your prime. What an incredible McGuffin that is; very, very powerful people would kill for it. And it's only a rank 3 seba. Wow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seba are really nice, but the main thing that made me love them it was their &quot;Fallen Star&quot; theme, I love the cosmic feel they have, they are the most unique of the Relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:50:39-08:00","id":310575,"title":"","content":"I love Seba, they're a handy excuse for anyone to have just about any kind of magical power you can think of. They remind me a bit of Goblin Vows in Changeling, in that if you need anything magical to happen not covered by existing rules, they're an easy shorthand.<br /> <br /> I was a bit confused that the ones listed in the book don't seem to have any real connection to art, however. I was expecting a few Seba to have an explicit connection to the art they are based on. A Seba that allowed you to perform a dance with magical properties, or let you cast a spell by painting, or imbued your voice with magical power. Each Temakh entry takes time to detail the kinds of art they look for in the production of Seba, but the example Seba all seem like examples of the cosmic type.<br /> <br /> I'm in the process of designing Seba for an upcoming Deceived game, and I'm trying to make sure that at least some of the products of artistic expression have powers that tie into their origins in some way. Revelations that require the suppression of the conscious self to activate, inspirations that need to be channeled through some kind of rhythm, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T15:28:12-08:00","id":310597,"title":"","content":"That does sound nifty, but I think perhaps the idea is that all art is just a medium that the cosmos reveals itself. Creating art is, to my own artist's understanding, acting as a vessel for your awareness of the universe, like it's passing through you.<br /> <br /> Anyway...a magical poem would belong to the Scribes and a magical painting would belong to the Builders, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T15:42:06-08:00","id":310602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310597#post310597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does sound nifty, but I think perhaps the idea is that all art is just a medium that the cosmos reveals itself. Creating art is, to my own artist's understanding, acting as a vessel for your awareness of the universe, like it's passing through you.<br /> <br /> Anyway...a magical poem would belong to the Scribes and a magical painting would belong to the Builders, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>A painting, as it is a representation of a thing,person or place would be an Effigy right?<br /> The Deceived are artists, but as a mean of how the cosmos reveal itself, as pure creation(essently the core of Nomenclature). They are about the revelation, vision, insight, inspiration etc, that comes to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:21:11-08:00","id":310660,"title":"","content":"Page 104, &quot;Manifest seba may be created spontaneously when a mortal artisan creates a masterful work of art, regardless of the specific media or performance involved. The resulting relics have a function that relates in some way to the aesthetic vision of the art that spawned them, but Fate dictates the specifics.&quot; Given the importance of aesthetics in relation to function, I can understand the confusion with effigies, but it's important to note that seba are never going to be physical even if generated by a physical thing. And based on the above principle, it doesn't seem out of the question to me that a song-based seba would use some element of song in its power, curse, and/or activation.<br /> <br /> On top of that, the rules for Keshina require the Deceived to find either a cosmic seba, or one based on the art appropriate for their Temakh. I'm not sure, at present, how on earth you're ever meant to tell the latter from any other manifest seba.<br /> <br /> As I gather it, a painting seba would not be the painting itself, it would be the idea the painting was seeking to express, the vision behind it. That doesn't mean its power has to be divorced from the act of painting, however. Take the Expression of Tutkepertanu as an example. Bearers of his Temakh have a power that allows them to paint with a magical technique, but it does not make the painting itself an effigy. The physical object is not where the power is. So a painting seba could be a seba that grants a power to its bearer enabling them to paint an ally, and in doing so give the ally some part of their own strength, to suggest one easy example.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another good example, as far as I can tell, would be the Scheming Bride from the opening fiction. From the brief details we can gather about it, it certainly appears to be trance-like in nature, both in the act of its activation and in its effect upon the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-12-2014, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T16:43:32-08:00","id":310701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310660#post310660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, the rules for Keshina require the Deceived to find either a cosmic seba, or one based on the art appropriate for their Temakh. I'm not sure, at present, how on earth you're ever meant to tell the latter from any other manifest seba.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the entire point of the Finding Seba rules on page 106:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Proxies for seba aren\u2019t quite like the proxies for other relics. Outside of other guildmates, the Deceived aren\u2019t apt to find people more likely to have seen or held a particular seba. <b>Instead, any artist who has ever created a masterwork (i.e., created art with an exceptional success) can potentially be chosen by Fate as a proxy to find a seba created via the same form of art.</b> How and why a particular artist is chosen by providence to offer clues to a seba\u2019s convergence, especially for artists with no personal connection whatsoever to the relic, is another of Fate\u2019s endless mysteries. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T17:37:47-08:00","id":310756,"title":"","content":"Ok, that certainly helps in those cases where the Seba isn't being divined or otherwise sought directly, but it's a rather roundabout way of figuring out the source of the Seba. And if you gain the Seba via some other method (slaying a previous owner, for example), there's really not any reason to continue following the scarab's path unless it is the Deceived's only recourse to determining the type of Seba they happen to have claimed.<br /> <br /> I just feel that integrating Seba into the various preferred means of expression (orations, revelations, visions, inspirations, trances, performances, and insights) via their mechanics adds a bit more flavour, while Cosmic Seba have powers that are more suited to fate and astrology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T18:33:59-08:00","id":310784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310756#post310756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that certainly helps in those cases where the Seba isn't being divined or otherwise sought directly, but it's a rather roundabout way of figuring out the source of the Seba. And if you gain the Seba via some other method (slaying a previous owner, for example), there's really not any reason to continue following the scarab's path unless it is the Deceived's only recourse to determining the type of Seba they happen to have claimed.<br /> <br /> I just feel that integrating Seba into the various preferred means of expression (orations, revelations, visions, inspirations, trances, performances, and insights) via their mechanics adds a bit more flavour, while Cosmic Seba have powers that are more suited to fate and astrology.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can certainly rule it this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.