e":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T23:45:03-08:00","id":310971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310951#post310951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sure to do a few that actually make use of the &quot;sacrifice for greater effect&quot; rules!<br /> <br /> I am really interested to see what you come up with, I must admit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wrote the sacrifice rules with several seba in mind, have no fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:48:50-08:00","id":310999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310957#post310957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cripes, how many pages are y'all adding?<br /> <br /> Of course, ancients need a <i>lot</i> of pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this notion. If Seba are getting expanded in general and True Name stuff is getting expanded in general, we are hopefully going to see a fair few extra pages in the final pdf version of Deceived. <br /> <br /> Now I'm really ticked my local group has written off Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:50:54-08:00","id":311003,"title":"","content":"We should start a club.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, a play group.(maybe, School keeps me busy, and I'm already in two games.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:56:31-08:00","id":311008,"title":"","content":"Tell me about it. I work security which has about the most unfriendly shift pattern you can imagine (4:30am starts). Even once I change jobs (happening soon) I'm going to be working 12 hour night shifts for at least 3 months (four on, four off). <br /> <br /> Its no coincidence that since getting into this industry I've not played in a game (not true, I joined a Pathfinder group about two months ago for a once a week thing) and had no time to run one. As a result I've got a load of things I want to run (around 10 games). Mummy was on the list until my local group just basically said &quot;not going to happen until 2E&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:01:11-08:00","id":311011,"title":"","content":"You know, last year I was all &quot;Oh, 2e, 2e, gotta play 2e&quot;, but now that I've had some time away from gaming, I gotta say it's a pretty ridiculous attitude. 1e has flaws, sure, but it's still perfectly serviceable. In the mean time, we have exactly 2.5 specific gamelines in 2e(I count the Hunter patch as the ,5). Way to limit game choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:08:11-08:00","id":311014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=311011#post311011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, last year I was all &quot;Oh, 2e, 2e, gotta play 2e&quot;, but now that I've had some time away from gaming, I gotta say it's a pretty ridiculous attitude. 1e has flaws, sure, but it's still perfectly serviceable. In the mean time, we have exactly 2.5 specific gamelines in 2e(I count the Hunter patch as the ,5). Way to limit game choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>My group has played a lot of NWoD in the 1.0 system. We have a few &quot;mechanical&quot; people who love to take systems apart and put them together again. Unfortunately said people have got so wrapped up in the flaws of the 1.0 system that they basically can't play a game in it anymore. Either because it makes them kinda angry or they just &quot;break the system&quot;. They have enough sway with the group (as they have the best system mastery, if not the best setting mastery) to pretty much get the group as a whole onboard this train of thought. <br /> <br /> At current the groups basically playing only one NWoD game which is a Changeling game &quot;hacked&quot; into 2E rules with a lot of homebrew. So selling something that is straight up 1E to them is just not going to work. This is unfortunate, but in the meantime it gives me a chance to appreciate Mummy as a setting, get back into some CWoD games I've not touched in years and await the 2E release of Promethean.<br /> <br /> What about you Arc? Is it just the time issue or does your local group have &quot;problems&quot; with Mummy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:26:38-08:00","id":311022,"title":"","content":"Right now, one of my groups has nWoD problems. In fact, I'll go and say that it has a &quot;anything but Masquerade and Ascension&quot; problem. I mean, they like the other ones? But the main head of it really has a hard on for Ascension and Masquerade. That's fine, but it's frustrating. I <i>think</i> i can inevitably win, since I got main head to like Changeling and Promethean, and I figure it's just a matter of time before I can get him into Demon and Geist and have the rest fall into place from there-but given the time matter and the mountain of ego and opinion, it's definitely a long fight. It's a shame too, because this is the best group I've played with so far, and while I like oWoD, there's a reason you all catch me here instead of those forums.<br /> <br /> As for my other group, we're going to be playing 2e to start off with(for good reasons that would take too long to explain), but after that,depending on what their schedule is like, it might become more mixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:29:18-08:00","id":311023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=311011#post311011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, last year I was all &quot;Oh, 2e, 2e, gotta play 2e&quot;, but now that I've had some time away from gaming, I gotta say it's a pretty ridiculous attitude. 1e has flaws, sure, but it's still perfectly serviceable. In the mean time, we have exactly 2.5 specific gamelines in 2e(I count the Hunter patch as the ,5). Way to limit game choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah because like, we have tons of gamelines that are already updated to 2e right? And the rules are soooo different from 1e. And Storytelling is all about the rules right? Yeah I don't understand this atitude either but what can you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:34:19-08:00","id":311025,"title":"","content":"I can get the attitude. 2e <i>is</i> a huge leap forward for the game, not only systematically but stylistically as well, and it's exciting, it's fun, it's shiny. I really, really wanted to take them for a test drive, which is why I pushed to play a game I wasn't quite prepared for(Moetsukiru: Hide and Seek, Blood and Smoke, Tokyo) with a group that wasn't prepared for me. Man, was that a lesson.<br /> <br /> The time since then has calmed me down on it, but I do understand the mentality-it's just silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:43:21-08:00","id":311029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=311003#post311003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should start a club.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, a play group.(maybe, School keeps me busy, and I'm already in two games.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I haven't been able to play Mummy either. Very difficult to find a WOD group with the same schedule as I here in Rio. It doesn't help that it hasn't been translated to Portuguese.Had the same problem with Geist.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T01:54:20-08:00","id":311032,"title":"","content":"So I'm writing a paper on The Things They Carried(doesn't everyone?),and I found this line loosely relevant. Loosely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tim O'Brien</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grief, terror, love, longing\u2014these were intangibles, but the intangibles had their own mass and specific gravity, they had tangible weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T02:01:53-08:00","id":311033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310952#post310952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so the cat's part-way out of the bag on the forthcoming bonus content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Doing the happy dance*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T19:48:42-08:00","id":313420,"title":"","content":"I'm a little over half through this. Been too busy with grad school to really sink my teeth into it until the past couple days.<br /> <br /> I will say this, the wait was 100% worth it. I'm hooked on everything in here.<br /> <br /> It also gave me some new energy for the 'basic' Arisen, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T21:42:13-08:00","id":313489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=311014#post311014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My group has played a lot of NWoD in the 1.0 system. We have a few &quot;mechanical&quot; people who love to take systems apart and put them together again. Unfortunately said people have got so wrapped up in the flaws of the 1.0 system that they basically can't play a game in it anymore. Either because it makes them kinda angry or they just &quot;break the system&quot;. They have enough sway with the group (as they have the best system mastery, if not the best setting mastery) to pretty much get the group as a whole onboard this train of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this. I don't like some of the gothic qualities that were jettisoned in 2E, like set lists classic virtues/vices, and derangements, and I was a little sad to see that BotD seems to rely somewhat on those particular core mechanics.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a lot of work to teach a group a new game in the first place, so I won't be hacking it into 2E when I run Mummy in a couple of weeks. My issues with nWoD 1.0 are fairly small and shouldn't negatively affect the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T04:56:41-08:00","id":313609,"title":"","content":"I give out experience points like beats, including the failure to dramatic failure option, and use the merit dot-pricing of the updates but that's all. Integrity is a better system in general but I'm a relatively lazy GM and <b>Mummy</b> needs a pretty complex karma meter.<br /> <br /> With that said, yeah <b>Mummy</b> took 1.0 and used it to the fullest. What a way to go out for the old system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T06:28:03-08:00","id":314416,"title":"","content":"The Unspeakable Name Affinity is probably one of the very best demonstrations of the &quot;master of the True Name&quot; thing. &quot;You think knowing my name gives you power over me? Oh no, it means part of me is inside you, and thus you'll never escape my reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> Regarding the Judges of Duat... according to the opening chapter the Shan'iatu definitely <i>wanted</i> to become Judges, but we have CAS's word that they didn't, let alone any evidence like number discrepancies. But the big rites at the end of Irem &quot;violated time&quot; - and the Shan'iatu lost a ton of their power over the Empire's course, enough that they had to take deliberate steps to prevent their human students from equalling them. So what if they misinterpreted things (or just fucked them up), and &quot;became&quot; the Judges in the same way that a human &quot;becomes&quot; a Promethean - ie being stripped for parts that are then made into something new. They made the Judges at the Empire's end - but that act of making reached back along their world-lines and leeched their power away for itself.<br /> Or maybe they <i>were</i> going to be the Judges, but squabbling over who'd be the bestest of the Judges annoyed Azar enough that he took the power and gave it to 42 others to be Judges instead (maybe 42 of the potential Arisen who were later thought not have made it through the Rite were actually given more important jobs).<br /> <br /> I wonder if Aset had anything to do with the founding of the Followers of Shulpae (well, I don't wonder as such, different line and all, but wonder if anyone else likes the idea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T13:14:41-08:00","id":314789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=314416#post314416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding the Judges of Duat... according to the opening chapter the Shan'iatu definitely <i>wanted</i> to become Judges, but we have CAS's word that they didn't, let alone any evidence like number discrepancies. But the big rites at the end of Irem &quot;violated time&quot; - and the Shan'iatu lost a ton of their power over the Empire's course, enough that they had to take deliberate steps to prevent their human students from equalling them. So what if they misinterpreted things (or just fucked them up), and &quot;became&quot; the Judges in the same way that a human &quot;becomes&quot; a Promethean - ie being stripped for parts that are then made into something new. They made the Judges at the Empire's end - but that act of making reached back along their world-lines and leeched their power away for itself.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes a lot of sense. It kind of mirrors the cyclical nature of the Descent in a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T09:29:12-08:00","id":315478,"title":"","content":"I think any previous discussion of &quot;the Judges&quot;, especially with the line developers, is now complicated by the fact that there were two sets of Judges (the Judges of Life and the Judges of Death) and we were previously never clear about which set we were talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T09:35:03-08:00","id":315481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=310365#post310365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I keep coming back to? The seba that lets you fully purge a person of all ailments and diseases, including old age. Are you 102, riddled with cancer, and on your deathbed? Not any more. Now you're hale, healthy, and in your prime. What an incredible McGuffin that is; very, very powerful people would kill for it. And it's only a rank 3 seba. Wow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But it only works, maximum, 10 times (statistically much less), and after the first two it runs a risk of immediately killing the patient. <br /> <br /> Which is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T15:39:23-08:00","id":315727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=315481#post315481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But it only works, maximum, 10 times (statistically much less), and after the first two it runs a risk of immediately killing the patient.<br /> <br /> Which is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the bearer is one of the Deceived and they're dampening the curse, in which case the price for failure is that the target number goes up and the patient is still on death's doorway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:14:59-08:00","id":315775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=315478#post315478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any previous discussion of &quot;the Judges&quot;, especially with the line developers, is now complicated by the fact that there were two sets of Judges (the Judges of Life and the Judges of Death) and we were previously never clear about which set we were talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know for sure that there are two sets? We know the Shan'iatu were trying to create &quot;Judges of Death&quot;, but we don't have any information on whether they succeeded and, as has been pointed out, it doesn't seem that the Judges we knew from before are a new creation. In fact, I feel reasonably certain that they are the original Judges. There's that brief mention, for example, that the Judges descend to Duat to judge souls, so the fact that the Arisen swore loyalty to the Judges in Duat doesn't seem out of place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=314416#post314416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding the Judges of Duat... according to the opening chapter the Shan'iatu definitely <i>wanted</i> to become Judges, but we have CAS's word that they didn't, let alone any evidence like number discrepancies. But the big rites at the end of Irem &quot;violated time&quot; - and the Shan'iatu lost a ton of their power over the Empire's course, enough that they had to take deliberate steps to prevent their human students from equalling them. So what if they misinterpreted things (or just fucked them up), and &quot;became&quot; the Judges in the same way that a human &quot;becomes&quot; a Promethean - ie being stripped for parts that are then made into something new. They made the Judges at the Empire's end - but that act of making reached back along their world-lines and leeched their power away for itself.<br /> Or maybe they <i>were</i> going to be the Judges, but squabbling over who'd be the bestest of the Judges annoyed Azar enough that he took the power and gave it to 42 others to be Judges instead (maybe 42 of the potential Arisen who were later thought not have made it through the Rite were actually given more important jobs).</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, I really like this theory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:36:26-08:00","id":315784,"title":"","content":"And what about the gods what are their roles in Mummy cosmology? There seens to be the 5 that represent the five-fould soul and Azar(my guess he used to represent the sahu). How do they differ from the Judges? We know a bit about Anpu but what about the others, what do they want? Do they preceed the Judges of Life, are they above them? Too many mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T04:22:45-08:00","id":316133,"title":"","content":"Part of it depends on how literally &quot;I was Sutek, but so were we all&quot; is meant to be taken. When I first read it, my initial impression was to take it straight. After all, the only other reference to Sutek is that he was supposedly Azar's brother whose rivalry led to Azar's death, and that his actions then enabled Azar's ascension and return to Heaven. However, we now have a much more concrete information on that event, and it could easily be supposed that these myths were just that, and that Sutek was an invention. And if the same goes for him, well, Anpu is really the only deity that has been independently verified to exist. Everything else could be the half-baked ramblings of guilty Shan'iatu spinning stories to cover up their shame.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure the first chapter also refers to Azar as &quot;the Judges' herald&quot;, insinuating that he might be lower (rather than higher, as the Shan'iatu would later claim to their mortal followers) than the Judges. At least, he was before he ascended the throne of Duat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T06:08:39-08:00","id":316187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=316133#post316133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure the first chapter also refers to Azar as &quot;the Judges' herald&quot;, insinuating that he might be lower (rather than higher, as the Shan'iatu would later claim to their mortal followers) than the Judges. At least, he was before he ascended the throne of Duat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also he was/contained the <i>axis mundi.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:03:14-08:00","id":316403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=315775#post315775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know for sure that there are two sets? We know the Shan'iatu were trying to create &quot;Judges of Death&quot;, but we don't have any information on whether they succeeded and, as has been pointed out, it doesn't seem that the Judges we knew from before are a new creation. In fact, I feel reasonably certain that they are the original Judges. There's that brief mention, for example, that the Judges descend to Duat to judge souls, so the fact that the Arisen swore loyalty to the Judges in Duat doesn't seem out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the Judges of Life were described (as basically emanations of the divine law of the universe) doesn't really seem to jive with the way the Judges who run the Arisen behave. And recall that the Shan'iatu didn't teach Irem about the Judges of Life, they taught their followers about the Judges of Death whom they planned to become. All the names Iremites know and use refer to <i>those</i> judges.You would expect some serious discrepancies between that dogma and the mummies' current orders/encounters with their judges if said mummies were interacting with the true, distant, &quot;good&quot; judges. You would *not* expect things like forced Descent rolls for trashtalking Irem (which, it seems, was a civilization erected by the Shan'iatu to subvert the intended order of the Judges of Life).<br /> <br /> And, I mean, you'd also expect them not to be such assholes.<br /> <br /> Also, the concept of ma'at (divine law, order-above-the-gods) is something the Judges of Life directly represent, but which the Arisen widely regarded as heretical when it arose in egypt (as mentioned in Guildhalls). And that sort of &quot;morality to which even the gods must adhere&quot; is pretty much what Apotheosis represents (&quot;There is a voice within your name that knows right from wrong&quot;). And pursuing apotheosis requires directly flouting &quot;your&quot; judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 11-19-2014, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:17:26-08:00","id":316411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=315727#post315727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the bearer is one of the Deceived and they're dampening the curse, in which case the price for failure is that the target number goes up and the patient is still on death's doorway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the fact that it detaches and becomes unbound isn't part of the curse. So you still lose it if you fail the roll. Though you're right, the patient gets to live. I forgot about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T22:28:32-08:00","id":316953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=316403#post316403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way the Judges of Life were described (as basically emanations of the divine law of the universe) doesn't really seem to jive with the way the Judges who run the Arisen behave. And recall that the Shan'iatu didn't teach Irem about the Judges of Life, they taught their followers about the Judges of Death whom they planned to become. All the names Iremites know and use refer to <i>those</i> judges.You would expect some serious discrepancies between that dogma and the mummies' current orders/encounters with their judges if said mummies were interacting with the true, distant, &quot;good&quot; judges. You would *not* expect things like forced Descent rolls for trashtalking Irem (which, it seems, was a civilization erected by the Shan'iatu to subvert the intended order of the Judges of Life).</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;names&quot; are an interesting point. After all, Name Magic needed to be used to create the Judges. The names the Shan'iatu planned to use weren't created until the Rite, and remember that just making up a name for Azar was something that struck them as, ahem, divine inspiration. Could be easy to assume that they desired to be the Judges, and didn't decouple their desire from what their desire was named. In other words, they used the names of existing Judges to describe the Judges they wished to become.<br /> <br /> The Descent rolls are an entirely separate matter. I'm of the belief that, if the Judges the Arisen are bound to are actually the real Judges, that has absolutely no bearing on their mission, Descent rolls, and other little quirks of their nature. They met the Judges because they died and went to Duat, where the original Judges are established as going to in order to pass Judgement on the dead anyway. It's called out in the corebook's GM section that the Judges have never once made a direct reappearance in the life of any of the Arisen since that first and only meeting in Duat.<br /> <br /> Also remember that, the same section I think, mentions that Arisen think magic cannot be used on a Mummy with the same Judge. They're wrong. It's Mummies who were made by the same Shan'iatu. The Judges they picked have no bearing on that part of their magic. It's a simple assumption, based on what the Shan'iatu told them, that the Judges hold the reigns over their descents.<br /> <br /> But the Shan'iatu lied when it came to Irem's cosmology, so everything the Arisen know on the matter is suspect.<br /> <br /> Basically, I wouldn't be surprised if the punishment for trash-talking Irem was not a Judge striking its servant for the disrespect, but rather a Shan'iatu (whatever form they now take) doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=316403#post316403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, I mean, you'd also expect them not to be such assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we know enough about the original Judges to be able to say definitively, one way or the other. Some of the crimes are nasty, but all we know is that these laws were apparently critical for purifying Sekhem for ascent into heaven. The morality of the laws is irrelevant, they're there as a function.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=316403#post316403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the concept of ma'at (divine law, order-above-the-gods) is something the Judges of Life directly represent, but which the Arisen widely regarded as heretical when it arose in egypt (as mentioned in Guildhalls). And that sort of &quot;morality to which even the gods must adhere&quot; is pretty much what Apotheosis represents (&quot;There is a voice within your name that knows right from wrong&quot;). And pursuing apotheosis requires directly flouting &quot;your&quot; judge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arisen regarded the concept as heretical because they'd been taught to regard it as heretical. By the Shan'iatu. Who lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T01:19:31-08:00","id":317102,"title":"","content":"Before the argument about if their are two sets of 42 Judges or a single set drags on I think its important to mention the following:<br /> <br /> <i>Its pretty obviously left vague so that the ST can make their own mind up about this idea. There is enough source material that can be interpreted in a variety of ways (as this discussion shows) that one can form their own opinion about it but no answer is given.</i><br /> <br /> While I do engage with the history of the Mummy setting (one has to really to run a game) I'm vary weary of treating it as any sort of meta-plot (which it is not).<br /> <br /> Its something that might be given a more definitive answer in future releases, until then I think its definitely in the &quot;make up your own mind&quot; camp of roleplay fluff (like the majority of &quot;facts&quot; in the NWoD).<br /> <br /> For my 2p I think there are two sets of Judges, but that purely an ascetic choice (I like symmetry in general and the Judges of Life/True Judges vs The Judge of Death/Shan'Iatu idea appeals to me as a result) on my part based off my take on the fluff presented in the various books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T01:30:43-08:00","id":317108,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think &quot;the Truth&quot; is too important for the purposes of actually running the game. I prefer to keep my revelations to the personal rather than the cosmological. I don't feel like &quot;There are actually two sets of Judges!&quot; is going to make much of an impact for players who care more about their characters than about the greater world. It would be interesting, to be sure, but I'm not all that invested about bringing much of it into my games.<br /> <br /> That said, going full paranoid towards the Shan'iatu and starting from the premise of &quot;everything is probably a lie&quot; is a lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T06:15:37-08:00","id":317330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=314416#post314416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unspeakable Name Affinity is probably one of the very best demonstrations of the &quot;master of the True Name&quot; thing. &quot;You think knowing my name gives you power over me? Oh no, it means part of me is inside you, and thus you'll never escape my reach.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. That was one of my favorite ones that I came up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:04:01-08:00","id":317609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=317108#post317108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't think &quot;the Truth&quot; is too important for the purposes of actually running the game. I prefer to keep my revelations to the personal rather than the cosmological. I don't feel like &quot;There are actually two sets of Judges!&quot; is going to make much of an impact for players who care more about their characters than about the greater world. It would be interesting, to be sure, but I'm not all that invested about bringing much of it into my games.<br /> <br /> That said, going full paranoid towards the Shan'iatu and starting from the premise of &quot;everything is probably a lie&quot; is a lot of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's relevant at least somewhat for mummies that are seeking apotheosis, because they're rebelling directly against....something. And whether that something is a Judge of Life, a Judge of Death, or something else will tend to affect how it reacts (and can react) to that rebellion. <br /> <br /> But you're totally right, all my reasons for assuming the Arisen answered to the Judges of Death kindof go away if we assume it's not any kind of Judge that's holding their leash. That it's just automatic programming or some trapped shan'iatu floating somewhere. Huh. Stuff to think on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T18:17:57-08:00","id":317842,"title":"","content":"When you've been enslaved for thousands upon thousands of years, endlessly performing hideous acts without question to achieve unknowable goals for taskmasters whom you never see and punish you more often than not...are you really going to be concerned with whether they're This or That?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T23:22:43-08:00","id":317990,"title":"","content":"...Yes.<br /> <br /> It's the closest any of the Deceived come to Apotheosis. It matters to them. And they are not so far removed from the Arisen to say it is irrelevant either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T00:16:17-08:00","id":318028,"title":"","content":"Nobody is saying the word &quot;irrelevant&quot;. But for the Arisen, for whom Apotheosis means the rejection of all supernatural overlords, the existence of a second (possible) set of Judges is just going to be another bunch of magical beings they no longer have an attachment to. It's not irrelevant. It's just... not very important. Many Arisen, particularly Ren Decree Mummies, will find the fact interesting, but for most the act of seeking Apotheosis is something intensely personal and so, necessarily, hidden truths about their personal lives are going to be a helluva lot more important than revelations about beings they met exactly once 6,000 years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T05:00:28-08:00","id":318165,"title":"","content":"It's important for mummies because what they are may be directly relevant to how they can be escaped (and the question of whether it's relevant can only be answered by knowing what they are). It's important for some of us as readers, because having such a truth has explicitly been posited as what sets Mummy apart from the other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T05:30:08-08:00","id":318174,"title":"","content":"Don't confuse my questioning of what is important in an actual game of Mummy with what I think is important to have in the books. Just as the broader details of the setting might not be all that relevant on the intensely personal level of characters in a game, the details of individual characters are obviously pretty irrelevant in a book about that very setting. I really enjoy the explorations into Mummy's cosmology (see not all that many posts ago with me going full-paranoid). The books are there to provide the context, which may or may not be important to the individual players and their characters. The players are there to provide the details of the game. Context can be useful there... but honestly, I just feel it's not as important as the characters.<br /> <br /> Hence my original point. When it comes to a big reveal moment, I prefer to reveal things about the characters and their personal lives, not the broader cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T09:00:12-08:00","id":318293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=318028#post318028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is saying the word &quot;irrelevant&quot;. But for the Arisen, for whom Apotheosis means the rejection of all supernatural overlords, the existence of a second (possible) set of Judges is just going to be another bunch of magical beings they no longer have an attachment to. It's not irrelevant. It's just... not very important. Many Arisen, particularly Ren Decree Mummies, will find the fact interesting, but for most the act of seeking Apotheosis is something intensely personal and so, necessarily, hidden truths about their personal lives are going to be a helluva lot more important than revelations about beings they met exactly once 6,000 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, considering that apotheosis for the arisen involves finding their own sense of right and wrong, and the &quot;true&quot; judges are supposedly the personifications of a universal moral guiding principle, it might matter because rejecting their &quot;false&quot; judge might lead them closer to the &quot;True&quot; judges. Rejecting a false and evil god doesn't necessarily have to involve rejecting all gods (I just lost like 5 atheist points for saying that, so I'm probably on infidel-probation). Especially for someone raised in a few thousand years of religion-as-a-facet-of-everyday-life, &quot;personal&quot; and &quot;theological&quot; are not necessarily as separate as you're implying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 11-21-2014, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T10:20:02-08:00","id":318340,"title":"","content":"Right: <i>supposedly</i> the personifications of moral principals. But it just seems, in practice out in the real <b>Mummy</b> world, that they just want to hoard a bunch of relics. I don't know.<br /> <br /> What did just occur to me, though, is why the Arisen gather relics for the <i>Judges</i> when, according to the latest supplement, the Rite of Return and relic-retrieval was set in place to gather relics for <i>Azar</i> as an apology","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T10:33:20-08:00","id":318355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=318340#post318340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right: <i>supposedly</i> the personifications of moral principals. But it just seems, in practice out in the real <b>Mummy</b> world, that they just want to hoard a bunch of relics. I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why the distinction, if it exists, might matter. My assumption was that the things holding the leash on the Arisen, and therefore demanding all those relics, were not the Judges of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T10:23:38-08:00","id":320012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=318340#post318340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right: <i>supposedly</i> the personifications of moral principals. But it just seems, in practice out in the real <b>Mummy</b> world, that they just want to hoard a bunch of relics. I don't know.<br /> <br /> What did just occur to me, though, is why the Arisen gather relics for the <i>Judges</i> when, according to the latest supplement, the Rite of Return and relic-retrieval was set in place to gather relics for <i>Azar</i> as an apology</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a case of the Shan'iatu not wanting to explain that whole debacle to their workers. The Relics could very well be presented to Azar after the Judges get them. Or the Shan'iatu completely failed another resolve roll and decided to keep the Relics to themselves. Either one works, the second could well be part of the Devourer's plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1965-joebobjoe","name":"joebobjoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T17:20:03-08:00","id":320262,"title":"","content":"Relics are literally the most ordered form of Sekhem out there, and the Judges of Life wanted humanity civilised in order to produce, well, ordered Sekhem. Could easily be going to them. Or it could be going to the Shan'iatu, to feed their existence in whatever state it is in now. Or the Judges of Death, if they do exist.<br /> <br /> I do think calling the Judges of Life moral is going a bit far from the source material though. I'd need to reread it, but my overwhelming impression was that they were personifications of order. Not morality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T19:47:57-08:00","id":320313,"title":"","content":"A cosmic order, yes. Law.<br /> <br /> Whether this order, this Law, is inherently moral is itself a value judgment left to us and our characters to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:04:22-08:00","id":320318,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Since the Temakh writing the opening chapter doesn't pass any kind of moral judgement on the Judges of Life (well, beyond calling them &quot;cruel&quot;, although that appears to be for reasons that may not necessarily apply from a human framework), it's entirely possible that the Judges of the corebook are the Judges of Life rather than, as Gabby put it, &quot;personifications of a universal moral guiding principle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:09:50-08:00","id":320321,"title":"","content":"Of course that also leaves us with the question of 'why is this the cosmic order? What purpose does punishing these sets of actions serve?'<br /> <br /> Fun questions to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:23:27-08:00","id":320325,"title":"","content":"The whole of civilisation was apparently a pre-existing idea the Judges handed down to the Shan'iatu to pass on to humanity. Why would such beings have any conceptualisation of human civilisation in an era of pre-history, and why did imposing it suit their ambition of making Sekhem more orderly?<br /> <br /> Aliens, obviously, are the only logical explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:50:34-08:00","id":320336,"title":"","content":"Don't be silly, Azahul. The Judges are the aliens.<br /> <br /> And apparently humans would have come up with civilization on their own. It's the magic and Sekhem stuff we needed help with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T21:03:45-08:00","id":320344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=320336#post320336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be silly, Azahul. The Judges are the aliens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was trying to say, yes.<br /> <br /> The interesting point was less that humans would have invented civilisation on their own, and more that the Judges handed the Shan'iatu a rather sophisticated cheat sheet of what civilisation entailed before anyone had actually done it.<br /> <br /> And also the fact that the Judges are aliens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T23:36:38-08:00","id":320520,"title":"","content":"Well the temakh had the power of Name. They invented the word 'King' before it had ever existed when they named Azar 'King of the Judges' or whatever. They probably Named 'Civilization' too before there had been any.<br /> <br /> But yes, in my head-canon the Shan'iatu are still aliens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T08:29:01-08:00","id":320743,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm not saying it's aliens, but it's aliens&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T08:36:52-08:00","id":320751,"title":"","content":"You know, it just occured to me we now have two BotD's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:36:27-08:00","id":320826,"title":"","content":"What's the other BotD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T10:03:04-08:00","id":320861,"title":"","content":"Book of the Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T10:21:47-08:00","id":320871,"title":"","content":"Huh. I thought that it was <i>Book of the Underworld</i>. Even stranger is that I have that book, and forgot its actual name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:49:39-08:00","id":320958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=320751#post320751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it just occured to me we now have two BotD's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everywhere I've talked about this book I've used &quot;BotDeceived&quot;. Not the most elegant solution, but at least it gets across what I'm trying to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T19:49:29-08:00","id":321324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=320958#post320958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everywhere I've talked about this book I've used &quot;BotDeceived&quot;. Not the most elegant solution, but at least it gets across what I'm trying to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just been saying &quot;Deceived&quot; without a definite article, to broadly the same effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T21:31:56-08:00","id":321396,"title":"","content":"BotDev? No confusion with BotD then...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:17:25-08:00","id":322271,"title":"","content":"I think just &quot;Deceived&quot; is a bit more elegant...<br /> <br /> Thinking on actually running the game, it strikes me that Deceived poses a very different set of questions to Mummy on a character level. I mean, the Memory system is absolutely integral to playing a Mummy. As you play you explore your own identity, who you have been, the deeds you have done, the depths to which you are capable of sinking, and so on. But Deceived... for all that they share the same Memory rules, it strikes me that this exploration of past identity is a lot more ancillary for them compared to the other aspect of their selves that looms large across the game. The Temakh, and each Deceived's relationship with their particular spirit shard, seems a bit more central to each character's identity than flashbacks and visions of the past.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else get the same impression? I've been sitting down to work out some basic flashbacks for my Deceived players, and it just doesn't seem quite as important for them as it is for my regular Mummy group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-25-2014, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T18:55:54-08:00","id":322331,"title":"","content":"The Deceived have been possessed by their temakh for so long that they've forgotten who they are. The relationship between Arisen and Judge concerning an Arisen's Memory is just as important as the relationship between Deceived and Temakh concerning the Deceived's Memory. Remember, too, that just as the Deceived-temakh relationship might admittedly be more central, the Deceived's Memory trait is also altered and adjusted for them with that in mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:06:27-08:00","id":322337,"title":"","content":"So you're saying that flashbacks and the like for Deceived should primarily focus on who the character is when they are/are not subsuming their own identity beneath that of the Temakh, contrasting the two cases against one another?<br /> <br /> I can probably roll with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T05:42:02-08:00","id":322733,"title":"","content":"Right. There's still a vestige of human personality in those possessed corpses. After all, they can achieve their own Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's like this: an Arisen who has learned that she murdered her entire cult is shocked to learn she was so blinded and deluded by her obedience to her Judge, but the Deceived who does a similar act would be shocked to learn that she was like a puppet dancing to some master's dance.<br /> <br /> Dance. Temakh. Pun. Did you see what I did there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T15:38:36-08:00","id":323206,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine they'd be shocked. I mean, it's not like the Deceived tend to forget that they have a Temakh riding around trying to pull their strings. But yes, it would certainly present an interesting quandary, particularly for a high Status character.<br /> <br /> I'm also increasingly fond of the idea of flashbacks that leave it ambiguous as to whether the character is following their Temakh's wishes or not. It'd be a fun twist to spring on a player who assumes they were driven to murder their cult because their Temakh was making them dance, only for it to be revealed that they actually did it of their own volition as a spiteful act against the Temakh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:14:48-08:00","id":323665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=305019#post305019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wondered if the woman that was sacrificed to take Azar to Duat eventually became the Isis analogue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's what she's named.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T11:36:36-08:00","id":325449,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading the first chapter and this book is already blowing my goddamn mind. 9/10 just from that first chapter.<br /> <br /> I think I'll need to re-read it a couple to times to digest everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:57:25-08:00","id":330898,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm still working my way through the book, although I've skimmed over it, but there is an idea that has struck me. Maybe the Judges of Duat don't serve Azar. Maybe they are Azar. Hear me out.<br /> <br /> The key number of judges is 42. Since there were 42 Shan'iatu, the idea that they became the Judges of Duat seems obvious, but BotD makes it clear that that never happened, since there are 35 of them that actually underwent the proper Rite of Return and spell to take them and Irem into Duat. The other seven, of course, got stuck becoming the Deceived. So what else appears in a cluster of 42? When the Shan'iatu killed Azar, they divided him into 43 parts, one for each of the Judges of Fate, plus one to bind Azar to this world. 42+1. Those 42 parts could have become the new Judges, while the 43rd part was consumed in an act of sympathetic magic to send the god to Duat. This seems to be backed up by the line in the core book that basically says that sacrifices to Ammut were needed to create the 42 judges. When the Shan'iatu divided Azar, they separated the different aspects of his soul. Over the course of the centuries, they unknowingly (or perhaps knowingly in the case of the 35) animated the different parts of his soul in Duat, turning them into lesser, but still extremely powerful, entities. Ammut benefits from these manipulations. She has removed her foe Azar from the land of the living and forever weakened him by manipulating his own children. She has likewise shamed and loosened the shackles of Apnu that bind her to Duat, allowing her to consume Skehem without as much interference. On top of that, she has now gained powerful, eternal, Lifeless servants in the land of the living. It is even possible that the 35 Shan'iatu who are not Deceived are complicit in this treachery. The Deceived were Azar's closest pupils and seek to restore him, even as they seek to retain all of the material goods that alienated them from him. The other Shan'iatu, on the other hand, were not nearly as close, and could have been persuaded by Ammut to fully and willingly betray their god, binding his power to Duat and then manipulating these new Judges to keep him there as their own puppet. It may even be possible that in Duat, Ammut and the Shan'iatu/Judges are now waging war against one another to control the realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T02:58:56-08:00","id":330939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=323206#post323206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't imagine they'd be shocked. I mean, it's not like the Deceived tend to forget that they have a Temakh riding around trying to pull their strings. But yes, it would certainly present an interesting quandary, particularly for a high Status character.<br /> <br /> I'm also increasingly fond of the idea of flashbacks that leave it ambiguous as to whether the character is following their Temakh's wishes or not. It'd be a fun twist to spring on a player who assumes they were driven to murder their cult because their Temakh was making them dance, only for it to be revealed that they actually did it of their own volition as a spiteful act against the Temakh.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've looked through the material and until now, I have yet to process why that was disturbing enough to put a warning sticker saying &quot;This is for mature minds&quot; on the book. At first glance, it's not pragmatic cold blood dripping in the closet of Vampire, not the hot savagery of Werewolf, not the &quot;hang yourself with the noose of your own creation&quot; of Mage. It has some of the Alienation elements of Promethean and strikes a massive cord with it's association with Changeling and Giest (just replace Giest with your Keeper and you're good).<br /> <br /> But I now realize the horror a bit: The Temakh is stuck in the old ways. Old hates, old methods, old notions. Slavery perfectly allowable, Old hatreds that never seem to die even though no living person participated in them (let alone know about them), Seeing the world evolve so fast beyond them and they thus feel entitled to burn the whole fucker down to start back from square one. Beyond even the petty squabbles that Kindred Elders have, for while their petty fights last centuries, the Deceived wage their fights across millenia both at each other and at civilization it's self.<br /> <br /> It's a crotchety old inhuman monster who can't let go of old hates and ideals turned genocidal terrorist because he hates civilization and that thing is in your head for eternity.<br /> <br /> All the while thinking that all these thoughts are of your own making until you die, and then it comes rushing back just what your identity truly is. Which is oh so brief before the monster that has you drags you back to the world of the living. To use Changeling terms, your own personal Keeper that you can never, ever, escape from. Only to have this process restart every time you awaken. A personal hell which is inflicted both on you and your cult. Forever. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:56:21-08:00","id":331536,"title":"","content":"Anyone had a chance to flick through the updated version of the book? The change to Blessed of the Black Stars is going to really, really please my player who took that Affinity. Two Black Die for a point of Ren.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit bummed that the short chapter fiction (the ones with the various Temakhs describing themselves) are still mostly missing the first line though. Is that just me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:01:24-08:00","id":331541,"title":"","content":"I never felt they were missing the first line at all actually...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:15:03-08:00","id":331546,"title":"","content":"You mean those truncated half-sentences that start a full line below the first line of the second paragraphs never struck you as odd? Particularly when there are two or three that actually do have the first lines?<br /> <br /> Or is this just something weird with the file I have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:47:07-08:00","id":331577,"title":"","content":"I think that might just be you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T16:53:58-08:00","id":331580,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Might have known.<br /> <br /> Ah well. The Black Die buff is pretty neat. Still a few things I remember pointing out in the errata that weren't changed though. The Leadership skill is still floating around on the sample Deceived in the Storyteller chapter, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:46:08-08:00","id":334697,"title":"","content":"So guys, according to the latest Morning Monday Meeting, Sothis is already on Editing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:52:42-08:00","id":334702,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the original plan for an October release for Deceived and a December release for Sothis?<br /> <br /> Deceived wasn't even all that late, so I'm not surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T21:04:02-08:00","id":334798,"title":"","content":"I will love them if they get that out before my next semester starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T04:18:34-08:00","id":335023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=334702#post334702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the original plan for an October release for Deceived and a December release for Sothis?<br /> <br /> Deceived wasn't even all that late, so I'm not surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Insert insane cackling)<br /> <br /> Yeah the plan was to have Deceived out in October <b>2013</b>...and that was the first revised date from July 2013.<br /> <br /> If we are talking 2014, Mummy had any rough estimated of release removed after DC was released(like the rest of the WoD). The GenCon book mentioned Deceived in the Autumn of 2014 (which happened) and Sothis in the Winter of 2015. So I am betting its likely to be late February or early March.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T04:59:12-08:00","id":335041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=335023#post335023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Insert insane cackling)<br /> <br /> Yeah the plan was to have Deceived out in October <b>2013</b>...and that was the first revised date from July 2013.<br /> <br /> If we are talking 2014, Mummy had any rough estimated of release removed after DC was released(like the rest of the WoD). The GenCon book mentioned Deceived in the Autumn of 2014 (which happened) and Sothis in the Winter of 2015. So I am betting its likely to be late February or early March.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends I guess. Depending how the editing goes and if Sothis get art directed ASAP maybe we won't have to wait much for layout and we can get it as early as late January.(Okay being very very optimistic here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T05:22:46-08:00","id":335059,"title":"","content":"Back before even <b>Guildhalls</b> was released the plan was for <b>Sothis</b> to be out by first half of 2014. But I think two books per year is a fair pace (<b>Core</b>/<b>Guildhalls</b>, <b>DC</b>/<b>Deceived</b>), and I'm more than happy with the quality of these books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T01:46:30-08:00","id":335896,"title":"","content":"Well certainly things seen to be pickin up speed now, so I'm not worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T21:38:04-08:00","id":348792,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, I've been reading the next chapter of the Avarice Chronicle and... it's a bit strange. The bit that really stands out to me is the finality with which it seems to treat an Arisen's death during the scenes at Sybaris. First, it was in regards to Akhomet's death by the Roller. Given the way Mummies work, the Roller could have killed her, consumed her body, and she would have simply undergone a Death Cycle and reformed around a canopic jar and/or been resummoned by her cult at a later date, rather than the the kind of destruction the story seems to imply has occurred. Death by Shuankhsen can certainly be hazardous, but that's due to the risk of returning as a Shuankhsen rather than the permanent ending implied in the text.<br /> <br /> On its own, I would simply put that down to some kind of power peculiar to the Roller. But in the next scene the Mummies are confronted by a chorus of seven Deceived, and it seems to think that if the Mummies don't behave in a civil manner and restrain themselves from fighting the Deceived then &quot;they will never be heard from again&quot;. Except... again, even the total destruction of their present bodies doesn't prevent them from just reforming around a canopic jar (probably on the other side of the planet) a few hours or days later.<br /> <br /> Anyone else a bit perplexed by this sample adventure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T01:03:19-08:00","id":348883,"title":"","content":"I get where you're coming from and this response partly feels like an ass-pull, but just because Mummies can come back from the dead doesn't mean that it's part of their Plan A strategy. You lose time, Sekhem, and Memory (I think?) - <i>none</i> of which are useless resources that you want to just throw away against Shuankhsen or Deceived. And maybe, after the core book adventure and the <b>Guildhalls</b> one, Mummy PCs are suspected to be a lower Sekhem, so it very well might be the end of their Descent should they die.<br /> <br /> And if you're like me that's extra bad because I use the option that it takes <i>years</i> for relics to recharge their resurrection power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T01:41:00-08:00","id":348890,"title":"","content":"&quot;The characters must negotiate with the Deceived, or they will never be heard from again.&quot;<br /> <br /> That wording doesn't exactly made me think, &quot;The characters must negotiate with the Deceived, or they will wake up somewhere else a few hours later. If they are close to the end of their Descents and perform particularly badly on their Death Cycles, they might even need to wait years.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's just really strange. The story seems to put a whole lot more gravitas on a Mummy dying than the mechanics do. Even at Sekhem 2, you have to perform badly on your Death Cycle for that to end your Descent. With Akhomat, she's Sekhem 3 and Memory 8. The Roller would have had to strip 2 Sekhem from her with his attacks (two separate attacks that each deal 3+ Aggravated damage) for her to be forced to the end of the Descent by that encounter. And even then, it's really bizarre that the Deceived makes a comment, &quot;So many centuries spent coming so close to Apotheosis, only to have it die.&quot;<br /> <br /> If she's spent centuries, another few years isn't going to bother her, surely? The PCs are even able to recover her relic, and presumably return it to her cult if they are so inclined.<br /> <br /> Although speaking of relics, bit funny that a Scribe has what sounds like an amulet for a relic. I wonder if there's a lot written on those rings...<br /> <br /> Also, no Memory loss for Sekhem drops. That comes at the end of the descent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T00:01:10-08:00","id":362174,"title":"","content":"Belated idle reskimming reminded me of a line that bears attention re: &quot;undying powers that broke time&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shan'iatu: &quot;Will the Rite of Return succeed? Will we become like the Judges, to master the Sekhem of Duat?&quot;<br /> Anpu: <b>It has already succeeded. It will always succeed.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:16:00-08:00","id":367488,"title":"","content":"How can you dream of opposing the Judges when <i>they are already here?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:53:52-08:00","id":367744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/303591-secrets-of-the-book-of-the-deceived?p=367488#post367488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you dream of opposing the Judges when <i>they are already here?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Stealing their Cairo Overcoat of Many Colors might be a good start, but that's exactly why an intelligent pseudoangelic being keeps a <b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">BACKUP COAT</span></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}